# Data extracted from EDAM_stable.owl
{"uri":"operation_0004","label":"Operation","definition":"A function that processes a set of inputs and results in a set of outputs, or associates arguments (inputs) with values (outputs)."}
{"uri":"operation_0224","label":"Query and retrieval","definition":"Search or query a data resource and retrieve entries and / or annotation."}
{"uri":"operation_0226","label":"Annotation","definition":"Annotate an entity (typically a biological or biomedical database entity) with terms from a controlled vocabulary."}
{"uri":"operation_0227","label":"Indexing","definition":"Generate an index of (typically a file of) biological data."}
{"uri":"operation_0230","label":"Sequence generation","definition":"Generate a molecular sequence by some means."}
{"uri":"operation_0231","label":"Sequence editing","definition":"Edit or change a molecular sequence, either randomly or specifically."}
{"uri":"operation_0232","label":"Sequence merging","definition":"Merge two or more (typically overlapping) molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0233","label":"Sequence conversion","definition":"Convert a molecular sequence from one type to another."}
{"uri":"operation_0234","label":"Sequence complexity calculation","definition":"Calculate sequence complexity, for example to find low-complexity regions in sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0235","label":"Sequence ambiguity calculation","definition":"Calculate sequence ambiguity, for example identity regions in protein or nucleotide sequences with many ambiguity codes."}
{"uri":"operation_0236","label":"Sequence composition calculation","definition":"Calculate character or word composition or frequency of a molecular sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0237","label":"Repeat sequence analysis","definition":"Find and/or analyse repeat sequences in (typically nucleotide) sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0238","label":"Sequence motif discovery","definition":"Discover new motifs or conserved patterns in sequences or sequence alignments (de-novo discovery)."}
{"uri":"operation_0239","label":"Sequence motif recognition","definition":"Find (scan for) known motifs, patterns and regular expressions in molecular sequence(s)."}
{"uri":"operation_0240","label":"Sequence motif comparison","definition":"Find motifs shared by molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0244","label":"Simulation analysis","definition":"Analyse flexibility and motion in protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_0245","label":"Structural motif discovery","definition":"Identify or screen for 3D structural motifs in protein structure(s)."}
{"uri":"operation_0246","label":"Protein domain recognition","definition":"Identify structural domains in a protein structure from first principles (for example calculations on structural compactness)."}
{"uri":"operation_0247","label":"Protein architecture analysis","definition":"Analyse the architecture (spatial arrangement of secondary structure) of protein structure(s)."}
{"uri":"operation_0248","label":"Residue interaction calculation","definition":"Calculate or extract inter-atomic, inter-residue or residue-atom contacts, distances and interactions in protein structure(s)."}
{"uri":"operation_0249","label":"Protein geometry calculation","definition":"Calculate, visualise or analyse phi/psi angles of a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_0250","label":"Protein property calculation","definition":"Extract, calculate or predict non-positional (physical or chemical) properties of a protein, including any non-positional properties of the molecular sequence, from processing a protein sequence or 3D structure."}
{"uri":"operation_0252","label":"Peptide immunogenicity prediction","definition":"Predict antigenicity, allergenicity / immunogenicity, allergic cross-reactivity etc of peptides and proteins."}
{"uri":"operation_0253","label":"Sequence feature detection","definition":"Predict, recognise and identify positional features in molecular sequences such as key functional sites or regions."}
{"uri":"operation_0256","label":"Sequence feature comparison","definition":"Compare the feature tables of two or more molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0258","label":"Sequence alignment analysis","definition":"Analyse a molecular sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0259","label":"Sequence alignment comparison","definition":"Compare (typically by aligning) two molecular sequence alignments."}
{"uri":"operation_0260","label":"Sequence alignment conversion","definition":"Convert a molecular sequence alignment from one type to another (for example amino acid to coding nucleotide sequence)."}
{"uri":"operation_0262","label":"Nucleic acid property calculation","definition":"Calculate or predict physical or chemical properties of nucleic acid molecules, including any non-positional properties of the molecular sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0264","label":"Alternative splicing prediction","definition":"Predict splicing alternatives or transcript isoforms from analysis of sequence data."}
{"uri":"operation_0265","label":"Frameshift detection","definition":"Detect frameshifts in DNA sequences, including frameshift sites and signals, and frameshift errors from sequencing projects."}
{"uri":"operation_0266","label":"Vector sequence detection","definition":"Detect vector sequences in nucleotide sequence, typically by comparison to a set of known vector sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0267","label":"Protein secondary structure prediction","definition":"Predict secondary structure of protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0268","label":"Protein super-secondary structure prediction","definition":"Predict super-secondary structure of protein sequence(s)."}
{"uri":"operation_0269","label":"Transmembrane protein prediction","definition":"Predict and/or classify transmembrane proteins or transmembrane (helical) domains or regions in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0270","label":"Transmembrane protein analysis","definition":"Analyse transmembrane protein(s), typically by processing sequence and / or structural data, and write an informative report for example about the protein and its transmembrane domains / regions."}
{"uri":"operation_0272","label":"Residue contact prediction","definition":"Predict contacts, non-covalent interactions and distance (constraints) between amino acids in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0276","label":"Protein interaction network analysis","definition":"Analyse a network of protein interactions."}
{"uri":"operation_0278","label":"RNA secondary structure prediction","definition":"Predict RNA secondary structure (for example knots, pseudoknots, alternative structures etc)."}
{"uri":"operation_0279","label":"Nucleic acid folding analysis","definition":"Analyse some aspect of RNA/DNA folding, typically by processing sequence and/or structural data. For example, compute folding energies such as minimum folding energies for DNA or RNA sequences or energy landscape of RNA mutants."}
{"uri":"operation_0282","label":"Genetic mapping","definition":"Generate a genetic (linkage) map of a DNA sequence (typically a chromosome) showing the relative positions of genetic markers based on estimation of non-physical distances."}
{"uri":"operation_0283","label":"Linkage analysis","definition":"Analyse genetic linkage."}
{"uri":"operation_0284","label":"Codon usage table generation","definition":"Calculate codon usage statistics and create a codon usage table."}
{"uri":"operation_0285","label":"Codon usage table comparison","definition":"Compare two or more codon usage tables."}
{"uri":"operation_0286","label":"Codon usage analysis","definition":"Analyse codon usage in molecular sequences or process codon usage data (e.g. a codon usage table)."}
{"uri":"operation_0287","label":"Base position variability plotting","definition":"Identify and plot third base position variability in a nucleotide sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0288","label":"Sequence word comparison","definition":"Find exact character or word matches between molecular sequences without full sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0289","label":"Sequence distance matrix generation","definition":"Calculate a sequence distance matrix or otherwise estimate genetic distances between molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0290","label":"Sequence redundancy removal","definition":"Compare two or more molecular sequences, identify and remove redundant sequences based on some criteria."}
{"uri":"operation_0291","label":"Sequence clustering","definition":"Build clusters of similar sequences, typically using scores from pair-wise alignment or other comparison of the sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0292","label":"Sequence alignment","definition":"Align (identify equivalent sites within) molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0294","label":"Structure-based sequence alignment","definition":"Align molecular sequences using sequence and structural information."}
{"uri":"operation_0295","label":"Structure alignment","definition":"Align (superimpose) molecular tertiary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0296","label":"Sequence profile generation","definition":"Generate some type of sequence profile (for example a hidden Markov model) from a sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0297","label":"3D profile generation","definition":"Generate some type of structural (3D) profile or template from a structure or structure alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0300","label":"Sequence profile alignment","definition":"Align molecular sequence(s) to sequence profile(s), or profiles to other profiles. A profile typically represents a sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0302","label":"Protein threading","definition":"Align molecular sequence to structure in 3D space (threading)."}
{"uri":"operation_0303","label":"Fold recognition","definition":"Recognize (predict and identify) known protein structural domains or folds in protein sequence(s) which (typically) are not accompanied by any significant sequence similarity to know structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0305","label":"Literature search","definition":"Query scientific literature, in search for articles, article data, concepts, named entities, or for statistics."}
{"uri":"operation_0306","label":"Text mining","definition":"Process and analyse text (typically scientific literature) to extract information from it."}
{"uri":"operation_0307","label":"Virtual PCR","definition":"Perform in-silico (virtual) PCR."}
{"uri":"operation_0308","label":"PCR primer design","definition":"Design or predict oligonucleotide primers for PCR and DNA amplification etc."}
{"uri":"operation_0309","label":"Microarray probe design","definition":"Predict and/or optimize oligonucleotide probes for DNA microarrays, for example for transcription profiling of genes, or for genomes and gene families."}
{"uri":"operation_0310","label":"Sequence assembly","definition":"Combine (align and merge) overlapping fragments of a DNA sequence to reconstruct the original sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0313","label":"Expression profile clustering","definition":"Perform cluster analysis of expression data to identify groups with similar expression profiles, for example by clustering."}
{"uri":"operation_0314","label":"Gene expression profiling","definition":"The measurement of the activity (expression) of multiple genes in a cell, tissue, sample etc., in order to get an impression of biological function."}
{"uri":"operation_0315","label":"Expression profile comparison","definition":"Comparison of expression profiles."}
{"uri":"operation_0319","label":"Protein secondary structure assignment","definition":"Assign secondary structure from protein coordinate or experimental data."}
{"uri":"operation_0320","label":"Protein structure assignment","definition":"Assign a protein tertiary structure (3D coordinates), or other aspects of protein structure, from raw experimental data."}
{"uri":"operation_0321","label":"Protein structure validation","definition":"Evaluate the quality or correctness a protein three-dimensional model."}
{"uri":"operation_0322","label":"Molecular model refinement","definition":"Refine (after evaluation) a model of a molecular structure (typically a protein structure) to reduce steric clashes, volume irregularities etc."}
{"uri":"operation_0323","label":"Phylogenetic inference","definition":"Construct a phylogenetic tree."}
{"uri":"operation_0324","label":"Phylogenetic analysis","definition":"Analyse an existing phylogenetic tree or trees, typically to detect features or make predictions."}
{"uri":"operation_0325","label":"Phylogenetic tree comparison","definition":"Compare two or more phylogenetic trees."}
{"uri":"operation_0326","label":"Phylogenetic tree editing","definition":"Edit a phylogenetic tree."}
{"uri":"operation_0327","label":"Phylogenetic footprinting","definition":"Comparison of a DNA sequence to orthologous sequences in different species and inference of a phylogenetic tree, in order to identify regulatory elements such as transcription factor binding sites (TFBS)."}
{"uri":"operation_0331","label":"Variant effect prediction","definition":"Predict the effect of point mutation on a protein structure, in terms of structural effects and protein folding, stability and function."}
{"uri":"operation_0334","label":"Enzyme kinetics calculation","definition":"Calculate Km, Vmax and derived data for an enzyme reaction."}
{"uri":"operation_0335","label":"Data formatting","definition":"Reformat a file of data (or equivalent entity in memory)."}
{"uri":"operation_0336","label":"Format validation","definition":"Test and validate the format and content of a data file."}
{"uri":"operation_0337","label":"Visualisation","definition":"Visualise, plot or render (graphically) biomolecular data such as molecular sequences or structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0338","label":"Sequence database search","definition":"Search a sequence database by sequence comparison and retrieve similar sequences. Sequences matching a given sequence motif or pattern, such as a Prosite pattern or regular expression."}
{"uri":"operation_0339","label":"Structure database search","definition":"Search a tertiary structure database, typically by sequence and/or structure comparison, or some other means, and retrieve structures and associated data."}
{"uri":"operation_0346","label":"Sequence similarity search","definition":"Search a sequence database and retrieve sequences that are similar to a query sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0349","label":"Sequence database search (by property)","definition":"Search a sequence database and retrieve sequences with a specified property, typically a physicochemical or compositional property."}
{"uri":"operation_0360","label":"Structural similarity search","definition":"Search a database of molecular structure and retrieve structures that are similar to a query structure."}
{"uri":"operation_0361","label":"Sequence annotation","definition":"Annotate a molecular sequence record with terms from a controlled vocabulary."}
{"uri":"operation_0362","label":"Genome annotation","definition":"Annotate a genome sequence with terms from a controlled vocabulary."}
{"uri":"operation_0363","label":"Reverse complement","definition":"Generate the reverse and / or complement of a nucleotide sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0364","label":"Random sequence generation","definition":"Generate a random sequence, for example, with a specific character composition."}
{"uri":"operation_0365","label":"Restriction digest","definition":"Generate digest fragments for a nucleotide sequence containing restriction sites."}
{"uri":"operation_0366","label":"Protein sequence cleavage","definition":"Cleave a protein sequence into peptide fragments (corresponding to enzymatic or chemical cleavage)."}
{"uri":"operation_0367","label":"Sequence mutation and randomisation","definition":"Mutate a molecular sequence a specified amount or shuffle it to produce a randomised sequence with the same overall composition."}
{"uri":"operation_0368","label":"Sequence masking","definition":"Mask characters in a molecular sequence (replacing those characters with a mask character)."}
{"uri":"operation_0369","label":"Sequence cutting","definition":"Cut (remove) characters or a region from a molecular sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0370","label":"Restriction site creation","definition":"Create (or remove) restriction sites in sequences, for example using silent mutations."}
{"uri":"operation_0371","label":"DNA translation","definition":"Translate a DNA sequence into protein."}
{"uri":"operation_0372","label":"DNA transcription","definition":"Transcribe a nucleotide sequence into mRNA sequence(s)."}
{"uri":"operation_0379","label":"Repeat sequence detection","definition":"Find (and possibly render) short repetitive subsequences (repeat sequences) in (typically nucleotide) sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0380","label":"Repeat sequence organisation analysis","definition":"Analyse repeat sequence organisation such as periodicity."}
{"uri":"operation_0384","label":"Accessible surface calculation","definition":"Calculate solvent accessible or buried surface areas in protein or other molecular structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0386","label":"Protein dipole moment calculation","definition":"Calculate whether a protein structure has an unusually large net charge (dipole moment)."}
{"uri":"operation_0387","label":"Molecular surface calculation","definition":"Calculate the molecular surface area in proteins and other macromolecules."}
{"uri":"operation_0389","label":"Protein-nucleic acid interaction analysis","definition":"Analyse the interaction of protein with nucleic acids, e.g. RNA or DNA-binding sites, interfaces etc."}
{"uri":"operation_0390","label":"Protein peeling","definition":"Decompose a structure into compact or globular fragments (protein peeling)."}
{"uri":"operation_0391","label":"Protein distance matrix calculation","definition":"Calculate a matrix of distance between residues (for example the C-alpha atoms) in a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_0392","label":"Contact map calculation","definition":"Calculate a residue contact map (typically all-versus-all inter-residue contacts) for a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_0393","label":"Residue cluster calculation","definition":"Calculate clusters of contacting residues in protein structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0394","label":"Hydrogen bond calculation","definition":"Identify potential hydrogen bonds between amino acids and other groups."}
{"uri":"operation_0396","label":"Ramachandran plot calculation","definition":"Calculate a Ramachandran plot of a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_0398","label":"Protein molecular weight calculation","definition":"Calculate the molecular weight of a protein sequence or fragments."}
{"uri":"operation_0399","label":"Protein extinction coefficient calculation","definition":"Predict extinction coefficients or optical density of a protein sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0400","label":"Protein pKa calculation","definition":"Calculate pH-dependent properties from pKa calculations of a protein sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0402","label":"Protein titration curve plotting","definition":"Plot a protein titration curve."}
{"uri":"operation_0403","label":"Protein isoelectric point calculation","definition":"Calculate isoelectric point of a protein sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0404","label":"Protein hydrogen exchange rate calculation","definition":"Estimate hydrogen exchange rate of a protein sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0405","label":"Protein hydrophobic region calculation","definition":"Calculate hydrophobic or hydrophilic / charged regions of a protein sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0406","label":"Protein aliphatic index calculation","definition":"Calculate aliphatic index (relative volume occupied by aliphatic side chains) of a protein."}
{"uri":"operation_0407","label":"Protein hydrophobic moment plotting","definition":"Calculate the hydrophobic moment of a peptide sequence and recognize amphiphilicity."}
{"uri":"operation_0408","label":"Protein globularity prediction","definition":"Predict the stability or globularity of a protein sequence, whether it is intrinsically unfolded etc."}
{"uri":"operation_0409","label":"Protein solubility prediction","definition":"Predict the solubility or atomic solvation energy of a protein sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0410","label":"Protein crystallizability prediction","definition":"Predict crystallizability of a protein sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0415","label":"Nucleic acid feature detection","definition":"Predict, recognise and identify features in nucleotide sequences such as functional sites or regions, typically by scanning for known motifs, patterns and regular expressions."}
{"uri":"operation_0416","label":"Epitope mapping","definition":"Predict antigenic determinant sites (epitopes) in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0417","label":"Post-translational modification site prediction","definition":"Predict post-translation modification sites in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0418","label":"Protein signal peptide detection","definition":"Detect or predict signal peptides and signal peptide cleavage sites in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0420","label":"Nucleic acids-binding site prediction","definition":"Predict or detect RNA and DNA-binding binding sites in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0422","label":"Protein cleavage site prediction","definition":"Detect or predict cleavage sites (enzymatic or chemical) in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0427","label":"Transposon prediction","definition":"Detect or predict transposons, retrotransposons / retrotransposition signatures etc."}
{"uri":"operation_0428","label":"PolyA signal detection","definition":"Detect polyA signals in nucleotide sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0429","label":"Quadruplex formation site detection","definition":"Detect quadruplex-forming motifs in nucleotide sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0430","label":"CpG island and isochore detection","definition":"Find CpG rich regions in a nucleotide sequence or isochores in genome sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0431","label":"Restriction site recognition","definition":"Find and identify restriction enzyme cleavage sites (restriction sites) in (typically) DNA sequences, for example to generate a restriction map."}
{"uri":"operation_0432","label":"Nucleosome position prediction","definition":"Identify or predict nucleosome exclusion sequences (nucleosome free regions) in DNA."}
{"uri":"operation_0433","label":"Splice site prediction","definition":"Identify, predict or analyse splice sites in nucleotide sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0435","label":"Operon prediction","definition":"Find operons (operators, promoters and genes) in bacteria genes."}
{"uri":"operation_0436","label":"Coding region prediction","definition":"Predict protein-coding regions (CDS or exon) or open reading frames in nucleotide sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0437","label":"SECIS element prediction","definition":"Predict selenocysteine insertion sequence (SECIS) in a DNA sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0438","label":"Transcriptional regulatory element prediction","definition":"Identify or predict transcriptional regulatory motifs, patterns, elements or regions in DNA sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0439","label":"Translation initiation site prediction","definition":"Predict translation initiation sites, possibly by searching a database of sites."}
{"uri":"operation_0440","label":"Promoter prediction","definition":"Identify or predict whole promoters or promoter elements (transcription start sites, RNA polymerase binding site, transcription factor binding sites, promoter enhancers etc) in DNA sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0441","label":"cis-regulatory element prediction","definition":"Identify, predict or analyse cis-regulatory elements in DNA sequences (TATA box, Pribnow box, SOS box, CAAT box, CCAAT box, operator etc.) or in RNA sequences (e.g. riboswitches)."}
{"uri":"operation_0443","label":"trans-regulatory element prediction","definition":"Identify or predict functional RNA sequences with a gene regulatory role (trans-regulatory elements) or targets."}
{"uri":"operation_0444","label":"S/MAR prediction","definition":"Identify matrix/scaffold attachment regions (MARs/SARs) in DNA sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0445","label":"Transcription factor binding site prediction","definition":"Identify or predict transcription factor binding sites in DNA sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0446","label":"Exonic splicing enhancer prediction","definition":"Identify or predict exonic splicing enhancers (ESE) in exons."}
{"uri":"operation_0447","label":"Sequence alignment validation","definition":"Evaluate molecular sequence alignment accuracy."}
{"uri":"operation_0448","label":"Sequence alignment analysis (conservation)","definition":"Analyse character conservation in a molecular sequence alignment, for example to derive a consensus sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0449","label":"Sequence alignment analysis (site correlation)","definition":"Analyse correlations between sites in a molecular sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0450","label":"Chimera detection","definition":"Detects chimeric sequences (chimeras) from a sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0451","label":"Recombination detection","definition":"Detect recombination (hotspots and coldspots) and identify recombination breakpoints in a sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0452","label":"Indel detection","definition":"Identify insertion, deletion and duplication events from a sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0455","label":"Nucleic acid thermodynamic property calculation","definition":"Calculate a thermodynamic property of DNA or DNA/RNA, such as melting temperature, enthalpy and entropy."}
{"uri":"operation_0456","label":"Nucleic acid melting profile plotting","definition":"Calculate and plot a DNA or DNA/RNA melting profile."}
{"uri":"operation_0457","label":"Nucleic acid stitch profile plotting","definition":"Calculate and plot a DNA or DNA/RNA stitch profile."}
{"uri":"operation_0458","label":"Nucleic acid melting curve plotting","definition":"Calculate and plot a DNA or DNA/RNA melting curve."}
{"uri":"operation_0459","label":"Nucleic acid probability profile plotting","definition":"Calculate and plot a DNA or DNA/RNA probability profile."}
{"uri":"operation_0460","label":"Nucleic acid temperature profile plotting","definition":"Calculate and plot a DNA or DNA/RNA temperature profile."}
{"uri":"operation_0461","label":"Nucleic acid curvature calculation","definition":"Calculate curvature and flexibility / stiffness of a nucleotide sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0463","label":"miRNA target prediction","definition":"Identify or predict microRNA sequences (miRNA) and precursors or microRNA targets / binding sites in a DNA sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_0464","label":"tRNA gene prediction","definition":"Identify or predict tRNA genes in genomic sequences (tRNA)."}
{"uri":"operation_0465","label":"siRNA binding specificity prediction","definition":"Assess binding specificity of putative siRNA sequence(s), for example for a functional assay, typically with respect to designing specific siRNA sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0468","label":"Protein secondary structure prediction (helices)","definition":"Predict helical secondary structure of protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0469","label":"Protein secondary structure prediction (turns)","definition":"Predict turn structure (for example beta hairpin turns) of protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0470","label":"Protein secondary structure prediction (coils)","definition":"Predict open coils, non-regular secondary structure and intrinsically disordered / unstructured regions of protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0471","label":"Disulfide bond prediction","definition":"Predict cysteine bonding state and disulfide bond partners in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0474","label":"Protein structure prediction","definition":"Predict tertiary structure (backbone and side-chain conformation) of protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0475","label":"Nucleic acid structure prediction","definition":"Predict structure of DNA or RNA."}
{"uri":"operation_0476","label":"Ab initio structure prediction","definition":"Predict tertiary structure of protein sequence(s) without homologs of known structure."}
{"uri":"operation_0477","label":"Protein modelling","definition":"Build a three-dimensional protein model based on known (for example homologs) structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0478","label":"Molecular docking","definition":"Model the structure of a protein in complex with a small molecule or another macromolecule."}
{"uri":"operation_0479","label":"Backbone modelling","definition":"Model protein backbone conformation."}
{"uri":"operation_0480","label":"Side chain modelling","definition":"Model, analyse or edit amino acid side chain conformation in protein structure, optimize side-chain packing, hydrogen bonding etc."}
{"uri":"operation_0481","label":"Loop modelling","definition":"Model loop conformation in protein structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0482","label":"Protein-ligand docking","definition":"Model protein-ligand (for example protein-peptide) binding using comparative modelling or other techniques."}
{"uri":"operation_0483","label":"RNA inverse folding","definition":"Predict or optimise RNA sequences (sequence pools) with likely secondary and tertiary structure for in vitro selection."}
{"uri":"operation_0484","label":"SNP detection","definition":"Find single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) - single nucleotide change in base positions - between sequences. Typically done for sequences from a high-throughput sequencing experiment that differ from a reference genome and which might, especially by reference to population frequency or functional data, indicate a polymorphism."}
{"uri":"operation_0485","label":"Radiation Hybrid Mapping","definition":"Generate a physical (radiation hybrid) map of genetic markers in a DNA sequence using provided radiation hybrid (RH) scores for one or more markers."}
{"uri":"operation_0487","label":"Haplotype mapping","definition":"Infer haplotypes, either alleles at multiple loci that are transmitted together on the same chromosome, or a set of single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) on a single chromatid that are statistically associated."}
{"uri":"operation_0488","label":"Linkage disequilibrium calculation","definition":"Calculate linkage disequilibrium; the non-random association of alleles or polymorphisms at two or more loci (not necessarily on the same chromosome)."}
{"uri":"operation_0489","label":"Genetic code prediction","definition":"Predict genetic code from analysis of codon usage data."}
{"uri":"operation_0490","label":"Dot plot plotting","definition":"Render a representation of a distribution that consists of group of data points plotted on a simple scale."}
{"uri":"operation_0491","label":"Pairwise sequence alignment","definition":"Align exactly two molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0492","label":"Multiple sequence alignment","definition":"Align more than two molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0495","label":"Local alignment","definition":"Locally align two or more molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0496","label":"Global alignment","definition":"Globally align two or more molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0499","label":"Tree-based sequence alignment","definition":"Align multiple sequences using relative gap costs calculated from neighbors in a supplied phylogenetic tree."}
{"uri":"operation_0502","label":"RNA secondary structure alignment","definition":"Align RNA secondary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0503","label":"Pairwise structure alignment","definition":"Align (superimpose) exactly two molecular tertiary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0504","label":"Multiple structure alignment","definition":"Align (superimpose) more than two molecular tertiary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0509","label":"Local structure alignment","definition":"Locally align (superimpose) two or more molecular tertiary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0510","label":"Global structure alignment","definition":"Globally align (superimpose) two or more molecular tertiary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_0523","label":"Mapping assembly","definition":"Sequence assembly by combining fragments using an existing backbone sequence, typically a reference genome."}
{"uri":"operation_0524","label":"De-novo assembly","definition":"Sequence assembly by combining fragments without the aid of a reference sequence or genome."}
{"uri":"operation_0525","label":"Genome assembly","definition":"The process of assembling many short DNA sequences together such that they represent the original chromosomes from which the DNA originated."}
{"uri":"operation_0526","label":"EST assembly","definition":"Sequence assembly for EST sequences (transcribed mRNA)."}
{"uri":"operation_0527","label":"Sequence tag mapping","definition":"Make sequence tag to gene assignments (tag mapping) of SAGE, MPSS and SBS data."}
{"uri":"operation_0531","label":"Heat map generation","definition":"Generate a heat map of expression data from e.g. microarray data."}
{"uri":"operation_0533","label":"Expression profile pathway mapping","definition":"Map an expression profile to known biological pathways, for example, to identify or reconstruct a pathway."}
{"uri":"operation_0538","label":"Phylogenetic inference (data centric)","definition":"Construct a phylogenetic tree from a specific type of data."}
{"uri":"operation_0539","label":"Phylogenetic inference (method centric)","definition":"Construct a phylogenetic tree using a specific method."}
{"uri":"operation_0540","label":"Phylogenetic inference (from molecular sequences)","definition":"Phylogenetic tree construction from molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0541","label":"Phylogenetic inference (from continuous quantitative characters)","definition":"Phylogenetic tree construction from continuous quantitative character data."}
{"uri":"operation_0542","label":"Phylogenetic inference (from gene frequencies)","definition":"Phylogenetic tree construction from gene frequency data."}
{"uri":"operation_0543","label":"Phylogenetic inference (from polymorphism data)","definition":"Phylogenetic tree construction from polymorphism data including microsatellites, RFLP (restriction fragment length polymorphisms), RAPD (random-amplified polymorphic DNA) and AFLP (amplified fragment length polymorphisms) data."}
{"uri":"operation_0544","label":"Species tree construction","definition":"Construct a phylogenetic species tree, for example, from a genome-wide sequence comparison."}
{"uri":"operation_0545","label":"Phylogenetic inference (parsimony methods)","definition":"Construct a phylogenetic tree by computing a sequence alignment and searching for the tree with the fewest number of character-state changes from the alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0546","label":"Phylogenetic inference (minimum distance methods)","definition":"Construct a phylogenetic tree by computing (or using precomputed) distances between sequences and searching for the tree with minimal discrepancies between pairwise distances."}
{"uri":"operation_0547","label":"Phylogenetic inference (maximum likelihood and Bayesian methods)","definition":"Construct a phylogenetic tree by relating sequence data to a hypothetical tree topology using a model of sequence evolution."}
{"uri":"operation_0548","label":"Phylogenetic inference (quartet methods)","definition":"Construct a phylogenetic tree by computing four-taxon trees (4-trees) and searching for the phylogeny that matches most closely."}
{"uri":"operation_0549","label":"Phylogenetic inference (AI methods)","definition":"Construct a phylogenetic tree by using artificial-intelligence methods, for example genetic algorithms."}
{"uri":"operation_0550","label":"DNA substitution modelling","definition":"Identify a plausible model of DNA substitution that explains a molecular (DNA or protein) sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_0551","label":"Phylogenetic tree topology analysis","definition":"Analyse the shape (topology) of a phylogenetic tree."}
{"uri":"operation_0552","label":"Phylogenetic tree bootstrapping","definition":"Apply bootstrapping or other measures to estimate confidence of a phylogenetic tree."}
{"uri":"operation_0553","label":"Gene tree construction","definition":"Construct a \"gene tree\" which represents the evolutionary history of the genes included in the study. This can be used to predict families of genes and gene function based on their position in a phylogenetic tree."}
{"uri":"operation_0554","label":"Allele frequency distribution analysis","definition":"Analyse a phylogenetic tree to identify allele frequency distribution and change that is subject to evolutionary pressures (natural selection, genetic drift, mutation and gene flow). Identify type of natural selection (such as stabilizing, balancing or disruptive)."}
{"uri":"operation_0555","label":"Consensus tree construction","definition":"Compare two or more phylogenetic trees to produce a consensus tree."}
{"uri":"operation_0556","label":"Phylogenetic sub/super tree construction","definition":"Compare two or more phylogenetic trees to detect subtrees or supertrees."}
{"uri":"operation_0557","label":"Phylogenetic tree distances calculation","definition":"Compare two or more phylogenetic trees to calculate distances between trees."}
{"uri":"operation_0558","label":"Phylogenetic tree annotation","definition":"Annotate a phylogenetic tree with terms from a controlled vocabulary."}
{"uri":"operation_0560","label":"DNA vaccine design","definition":"Predict or optimise DNA to elicit (via DNA vaccination) an immunological response."}
{"uri":"operation_0564","label":"Sequence visualisation","definition":"Visualise, format or render a molecular sequence or sequences such as a sequence alignment, possibly with sequence features or properties shown."}
{"uri":"operation_0566","label":"Sequence cluster visualisation","definition":"Visualise, format or render sequence clusters."}
{"uri":"operation_0567","label":"Phylogenetic tree visualisation","definition":"Render or visualise a phylogenetic tree."}
{"uri":"operation_0570","label":"Structure visualisation","definition":"Visualise or render molecular 3D structure, for example a high-quality static picture or animation."}
{"uri":"operation_0571","label":"Expression data visualisation","definition":"Visualise microarray or other expression data."}
{"uri":"operation_0573","label":"Map drawing","definition":"Draw or visualise a DNA map."}
{"uri":"operation_0575","label":"Restriction map drawing","definition":"Draw or visualise restriction maps in DNA sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_0578","label":"Plasmid map drawing","definition":"Draw a circular maps of DNA, for example a plasmid map."}
{"uri":"operation_0579","label":"Operon drawing","definition":"Visualise operon structure etc."}
{"uri":"operation_1777","label":"Protein function prediction","definition":"Predict the biological or biochemical role of a protein, or other aspects of a protein function."}
{"uri":"operation_1778","label":"Protein function comparison","definition":"Compare the functional properties of two or more proteins."}
{"uri":"operation_1781","label":"Gene regulatory network analysis","definition":"Analyse a known network of gene regulation."}
{"uri":"operation_1812","label":"Data parsing","definition":"Parse, prepare or load a user-specified data file so that it is available for use."}
{"uri":"operation_1816","label":"Surface rendering","definition":"Calculate the positions of dots that are homogeneously distributed over the surface of a molecule."}
{"uri":"operation_1829","label":"Cysteine bridge detection","definition":"Detect cysteine bridges (from coordinate data) in a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_1830","label":"Free cysteine detection","definition":"Detect free cysteines in a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_1831","label":"Metal-bound cysteine detection","definition":"Detect cysteines that are bound to metal in a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_1834","label":"Protein-metal contact calculation","definition":"Calculate protein residue contacts with metal in a structure."}
{"uri":"operation_1836","label":"Residue bump detection","definition":"Detect 'bumps' between residues in a structure, i.e. those with pairs of atoms whose Van der Waals' radii interpenetrate more than a defined distance."}
{"uri":"operation_1839","label":"Salt bridge calculation","definition":"Calculate (and possibly score) salt bridges in a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_1843","label":"Residue packing validation","definition":"Identify poorly packed residues in protein structures."}
{"uri":"operation_1844","label":"Protein geometry validation","definition":"Validate protein geometry, for example bond lengths, bond angles, torsion angles, chiralities, planaraties etc. An example is validation of a Ramachandran plot of a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_1850","label":"Protein cysteine and disulfide bond assignment","definition":"Assign cysteine bonding state and disulfide bond partners in protein structures."}
{"uri":"operation_2008","label":"siRNA duplex prediction","definition":"Identify or predict siRNA duplexes in RNA."}
{"uri":"operation_2089","label":"Sequence alignment refinement","definition":"Refine an existing sequence alignment."}
{"uri":"operation_2121","label":"Sequence file editing","definition":"Perform basic (non-analytical) operations on a report or file of sequences (which might include features), such as file concatenation, removal or ordering of sequences, creation of subset or a new file of sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_2233","label":"Representative sequence identification","definition":"Identify a representative sequence from a set of sequences, typically using scores from pair-wise alignment or other comparison of the sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_2238","label":"Statistical calculation","definition":"Perform a statistical data operation of some type, e.g. calibration or validation."}
{"uri":"operation_2239","label":"3D-1D scoring matrix generation","definition":"Calculate a 3D-1D scoring matrix from analysis of protein sequence and structural data."}
{"uri":"operation_2241","label":"Transmembrane protein visualisation","definition":"Visualise transmembrane proteins, typically the transmembrane regions within a sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_2284","label":"Nucleic acid density plotting","definition":"Calculate a density plot (of base composition) for a nucleotide sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_2403","label":"Sequence analysis","definition":"Analyse one or more known molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_2404","label":"Sequence motif analysis","definition":"Analyse molecular sequence motifs."}
{"uri":"operation_2406","label":"Protein structure analysis","definition":"Analyse protein structural data."}
{"uri":"operation_2409","label":"Data handling","definition":"Basic (non-analytical) operations of some data, either a file or equivalent entity in memory, such that the same basic type of data is consumed as input and generated as output."}
{"uri":"operation_2415","label":"Protein folding analysis","definition":"Analyse, simulate or predict protein folding, typically by processing sequence and / or structural data. For example, predict sites of nucleation or stabilisation key to protein folding."}
{"uri":"operation_2416","label":"Protein secondary structure analysis","definition":"Analyse protein secondary structure data."}
{"uri":"operation_2419","label":"Primer and probe design","definition":"Predict oligonucleotide primers or probes."}
{"uri":"operation_2421","label":"Database search","definition":"Search a database (or other data resource) with a supplied query and retrieve entries (or parts of entries) that are similar to the query."}
{"uri":"operation_2422","label":"Data retrieval","definition":"Retrieve an entry (or part of an entry) from a data resource that matches a supplied query. This might include some primary data and annotation. The query is a data identifier or other indexed term. For example, retrieve a sequence record with the specified accession number, or matching supplied keywords."}
{"uri":"operation_2423","label":"Prediction and recognition","definition":"Predict, recognise, detect or identify some properties of a biomolecule."}
{"uri":"operation_2424","label":"Comparison","definition":"Compare two or more things to identify similarities."}
{"uri":"operation_2425","label":"Optimisation and refinement","definition":"Refine or optimise some data model."}
{"uri":"operation_2426","label":"Modelling and simulation","definition":"Model or simulate some biological entity or system, typically using mathematical techniques including dynamical systems, statistical models, differential equations, and game theoretic models."}
{"uri":"operation_2428","label":"Validation","definition":"Validate some data."}
{"uri":"operation_2429","label":"Mapping","definition":"Map properties to positions on an biological entity (typically a molecular sequence or structure), or assemble such an entity from constituent parts."}
{"uri":"operation_2430","label":"Design","definition":"Design a biological entity (typically a molecular sequence or structure) with specific properties."}
{"uri":"operation_2436","label":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","definition":"Identify classes of genes or proteins that are over or under-represented in a large set of genes or proteins. For example analysis of a set of genes corresponding to a gene expression profile, annotated with Gene Ontology (GO) concepts, where eventual over-/under-representation of certain GO concept within the studied set of genes is revealed."}
{"uri":"operation_2437","label":"Gene regulatory network prediction","definition":"Predict a network of gene regulation."}
{"uri":"operation_2439","label":"RNA secondary structure analysis","definition":"Process (read and / or write) RNA secondary structure data."}
{"uri":"operation_2441","label":"RNA structure prediction","definition":"Predict RNA tertiary structure."}
{"uri":"operation_2442","label":"DNA structure prediction","definition":"Predict DNA tertiary structure."}
{"uri":"operation_2451","label":"Sequence comparison","definition":"Compare two or more molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_2454","label":"Gene prediction","definition":"Detect, predict and identify genes or components of genes in DNA sequences, including promoters, coding regions, splice sites, etc."}
{"uri":"operation_2464","label":"Protein-protein binding site prediction","definition":"Identify or predict protein-protein binding sites."}
{"uri":"operation_2474","label":"Protein architecture comparison","definition":"Compare the architecture of two or more protein structures."}
{"uri":"operation_2475","label":"Protein architecture recognition","definition":"Identify the architecture of a protein structure."}
{"uri":"operation_2476","label":"Molecular dynamics","definition":"The simulation of molecular (typically protein) conformation using a computational model of physical forces and computer simulation."}
{"uri":"operation_2478","label":"Nucleic acid sequence analysis","definition":"Analyse a nucleic acid sequence (using methods that are only applicable to nucleic acid sequences)."}
{"uri":"operation_2479","label":"Protein sequence analysis","definition":"Analyse a protein sequence (using methods that are only applicable to protein sequences)."}
{"uri":"operation_2480","label":"Structure analysis","definition":"Analyse known molecular tertiary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_2481","label":"Nucleic acid structure analysis","definition":"Analyse nucleic acid tertiary structural data."}
{"uri":"operation_2483","label":"Structure comparison","definition":"Compare two or more molecular tertiary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_2485","label":"Helical wheel drawing","definition":"Render a helical wheel representation of protein secondary structure."}
{"uri":"operation_2486","label":"Topology diagram drawing","definition":"Render a topology diagram of protein secondary structure."}
{"uri":"operation_2487","label":"Protein structure comparison","definition":"Compare protein tertiary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_2488","label":"Protein secondary structure comparison","definition":"Compare protein secondary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_2489","label":"Subcellular localisation prediction","definition":"Predict the subcellular localisation of a protein sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_2492","label":"Protein interaction prediction","definition":"Predict the interactions of proteins with other proteins."}
{"uri":"operation_2495","label":"Expression analysis","definition":"Process (read and/or write) expression data from experiments measuring molecules (e.g. omics data), including analysis of one or more expression profiles, typically to interpret them in functional terms."}
{"uri":"operation_2499","label":"Splicing analysis","definition":"Predict, analyse, characterize or model splice sites, splicing events and so on, typically by comparing multiple nucleic acid sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_2510","label":"DNA back-translation","definition":"Back-translate a protein sequence into DNA."}
{"uri":"operation_2518","label":"Nucleic acid structure comparison","definition":"Compare nucleic acid tertiary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_2520","label":"DNA mapping","definition":"Generate a map of a DNA sequence annotated with positional or non-positional features of some type."}
{"uri":"operation_2574","label":"Protein hydropathy calculation","definition":"Analyse the hydrophobic, hydrophilic or charge properties of a protein (from analysis of sequence or structural information)."}
{"uri":"operation_2575","label":"Binding site prediction","definition":"Identify or predict catalytic residues, active sites or other ligand-binding sites in protein sequences or structures."}
{"uri":"operation_2844","label":"Structure clustering","definition":"Build clusters of similar structures, typically using scores from structural alignment methods."}
{"uri":"operation_2871","label":"Sequence tagged site (STS) mapping","definition":"Generate a physical DNA map (sequence map) from analysis of sequence tagged sites (STS)."}
{"uri":"operation_2928","label":"Alignment","definition":"Compare two or more entities, typically the sequence or structure (or derivatives) of macromolecules, to identify equivalent subunits."}
{"uri":"operation_2929","label":"Protein fragment weight comparison","definition":"Calculate the molecular weight of a protein (or fragments) and compare it to another protein or reference data. Generally used for protein identification."}
{"uri":"operation_2930","label":"Protein property comparison","definition":"Compare the physicochemical properties of two or more proteins (or reference data)."}
{"uri":"operation_2935","label":"Clustering profile plotting","definition":"Visualise clustered quantitative data as set of different profiles, where each profile is plotted versus different entities or samples on the X-axis."}
{"uri":"operation_2937","label":"Proximity map plotting","definition":"Generate a plot of distances (distance or correlation matrix) between expression values."}
{"uri":"operation_2938","label":"Dendrogram visualisation","definition":"Visualise clustered expression data using a tree diagram."}
{"uri":"operation_2939","label":"Principal component visualisation","definition":"Visualize the results of a principal component analysis (orthogonal data transformation). For example, visualization of the principal components (essential subspace) coming from a Principal Component Analysis (PCA) on the trajectory atomistic coordinates of a molecular structure."}
{"uri":"operation_2940","label":"Scatter plot plotting","definition":"Render a graph in which the values of two variables are plotted along two axes; the pattern of the points reveals any correlation."}
{"uri":"operation_2942","label":"Treemap visualisation","definition":"Visualise gene expression data after hierarchical clustering for representing hierarchical relationships."}
{"uri":"operation_2943","label":"Box-Whisker plot plotting","definition":"Generate a box plot, i.e. a depiction of groups of numerical data through their quartiles."}
{"uri":"operation_2944","label":"Physical mapping","definition":"Generate a physical (sequence) map of a DNA sequence showing the physical distance (base pairs) between features or landmarks such as restriction sites, cloned DNA fragments, genes and other genetic markers."}
{"uri":"operation_2945","label":"Data analysis","definition":"Apply analytical methods to existing data of a specific type."}
{"uri":"operation_2949","label":"Protein-protein interaction analysis","definition":"Analyse the interactions of proteins with other proteins."}
{"uri":"operation_2950","label":"Residue distance calculation","definition":"Calculate contacts between residues, or between residues and other groups, in a protein structure, on the basis of distance calculations."}
{"uri":"operation_2962","label":"Codon usage bias calculation","definition":"Calculate codon usage bias, e.g. generate a codon usage bias plot."}
{"uri":"operation_2964","label":"Codon usage fraction calculation","definition":"Calculate the differences in codon usage fractions between two sequences, sets of sequences, codon usage tables etc."}
{"uri":"operation_2990","label":"Classification","definition":"Assign molecular sequences, structures or other biological data to a specific group or category according to qualities it shares with that group or category."}
{"uri":"operation_2995","label":"Sequence classification","definition":"Assign molecular sequence(s) to a group or category."}
{"uri":"operation_2996","label":"Structure classification","definition":"Assign molecular structure(s) to a group or category."}
{"uri":"operation_2997","label":"Protein comparison","definition":"Compare two or more proteins (or some aspect) to identify similarities."}
{"uri":"operation_2998","label":"Nucleic acid comparison","definition":"Compare two or more nucleic acids to identify similarities."}
{"uri":"operation_3080","label":"Structure editing","definition":"Edit, convert or otherwise change a molecular tertiary structure, either randomly or specifically."}
{"uri":"operation_3081","label":"Sequence alignment editing","definition":"Edit, convert or otherwise change a molecular sequence alignment, either randomly or specifically."}
{"uri":"operation_3092","label":"Protein feature detection","definition":"Predict, recognise and identify positional features in proteins from analysing protein sequences or structures."}
{"uri":"operation_3094","label":"Protein interaction network prediction","definition":"Predict a network of protein interactions."}
{"uri":"operation_3095","label":"Nucleic acid design","definition":"Design (or predict) nucleic acid sequences with specific chemical or physical properties."}
{"uri":"operation_3096","label":"Data editing","definition":"Edit a data entity, either randomly or specifically."}
{"uri":"operation_3180","label":"Sequence assembly validation","definition":"Evaluate a DNA sequence assembly, typically for purposes of quality control."}
{"uri":"operation_3182","label":"Genome alignment","definition":"Align two or more (typically huge) molecular sequences that represent genomes."}
{"uri":"operation_3183","label":"Localised reassembly","definition":"Reconstruction of a sequence assembly in a localised area."}
{"uri":"operation_3184","label":"Sequence assembly visualisation","definition":"Render and visualise a DNA sequence assembly."}
{"uri":"operation_3185","label":"Base-calling","definition":"Identify base (nucleobase) sequence from a fluorescence 'trace' data generated by an automated DNA sequencer."}
{"uri":"operation_3186","label":"Bisulfite mapping","definition":"The mapping of methylation sites in a DNA (genome) sequence. Typically, the mapping of high-throughput bisulfite reads to the reference genome."}
{"uri":"operation_3187","label":"Sequence contamination filtering","definition":"Identify and filter a (typically large) sequence data set to remove sequences from contaminants in the sample that was sequenced."}
{"uri":"operation_3192","label":"Sequence trimming","definition":"Cut (remove) the end from a molecular sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_3194","label":"Genome feature comparison","definition":"Compare the features of two genome sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_3195","label":"Sequencing error detection","definition":"Detect errors in DNA sequences generated from sequencing projects)."}
{"uri":"operation_3196","label":"Genotyping","definition":"Analyse DNA sequence data to identify differences between the genetic composition (genotype) of an individual compared to other individual's or a reference sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_3197","label":"Genetic variation analysis","definition":"Analyse a genetic variation, for example to annotate its location, alleles, classification, and effects on individual transcripts predicted for a gene model."}
{"uri":"operation_3198","label":"Read mapping","definition":"Align short oligonucleotide sequences (reads) to a larger (genomic) sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_3199","label":"Split read mapping","definition":"A variant of oligonucleotide mapping where a read is mapped to two separate locations because of possible structural variation."}
{"uri":"operation_3200","label":"DNA barcoding","definition":"Analyse DNA sequences in order to identify a DNA 'barcode'; marker genes or any short fragment(s) of DNA that are useful to diagnose the taxa of biological organisms."}
{"uri":"operation_3203","label":"Chromatogram visualisation","definition":"Visualise, format or render an image of a Chromatogram."}
{"uri":"operation_3204","label":"Methylation analysis","definition":"Analyse cytosine methylation states in nucleic acid sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_3206","label":"Whole genome methylation analysis","definition":"Measure the overall level of methyl cytosines in a genome from analysis of experimental data, typically from chromatographic methods and methyl accepting capacity assay."}
{"uri":"operation_3207","label":"Gene methylation analysis","definition":"Analysing the DNA methylation of specific genes or regions of interest."}
{"uri":"operation_3208","label":"Genome visualisation","definition":"Visualise, format or render a nucleic acid sequence that is part of (and in context of) a complete genome sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_3209","label":"Genome comparison","definition":"Compare the sequence or features of two or more genomes, for example, to find matching regions."}
{"uri":"operation_3211","label":"Genome indexing","definition":"Generate an index of a genome sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_3214","label":"Spectral analysis","definition":"Analyse one or more spectra from mass spectrometry (or other) experiments."}
{"uri":"operation_3215","label":"Peak detection","definition":"Identify peaks in a spectrum from a mass spectrometry, NMR, or some other spectrum-generating experiment."}
{"uri":"operation_3216","label":"Scaffolding","definition":"Link together a non-contiguous series of genomic sequences into a scaffold, consisting of sequences separated by gaps of known length. The sequences that are linked are typically typically contigs; contiguous sequences corresponding to read overlaps."}
{"uri":"operation_3217","label":"Scaffold gap completion","definition":"Fill the gaps in a sequence assembly (scaffold) by merging in additional sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_3218","label":"Sequencing quality control","definition":"Raw sequence data quality control."}
{"uri":"operation_3219","label":"Read pre-processing","definition":"Pre-process sequence reads to ensure (or improve) quality and reliability."}
{"uri":"operation_3221","label":"Species frequency estimation","definition":"Estimate the frequencies of different species from analysis of the molecular sequences, typically of DNA recovered from environmental samples."}
{"uri":"operation_3222","label":"Peak calling","definition":"Identify putative protein-binding regions in a genome sequence from analysis of Chip-sequencing data or ChIP-on-chip data."}
{"uri":"operation_3223","label":"Differential gene expression profiling","definition":"Identify from molecular sequence analysis (typically from analysis of microarray or RNA-seq data) genes whose expression levels are significantly different between two sample groups."}
{"uri":"operation_3225","label":"Variant classification","definition":"Classify variants based on their potential effect on genes, especially functional effects on the expressed proteins."}
{"uri":"operation_3226","label":"Variant prioritisation","definition":"Identify biologically interesting variants by prioritizing individual variants, for example, homozygous variants absent in control genomes."}
{"uri":"operation_3227","label":"Variant calling","definition":"Detect, identify and map mutations, such as single nucleotide polymorphisms, short indels and structural variants, in multiple DNA sequences. Typically the alignment and comparison of the fluorescent traces produced by DNA sequencing hardware, to study genomic alterations."}
{"uri":"operation_3228","label":"Structural variation detection","definition":"Detect large regions in a genome subject to copy-number variation, or other structural variations in genome(s)."}
{"uri":"operation_3229","label":"Exome assembly","definition":"Analyse sequencing data from experiments aiming to selectively sequence the coding regions of the genome."}
{"uri":"operation_3230","label":"Read depth analysis","definition":"Analyse mapping density (read depth) of (typically) short reads from sequencing platforms, for example, to detect deletions and duplications."}
{"uri":"operation_3232","label":"Gene expression QTL analysis","definition":"Combine classical quantitative trait loci (QTL) analysis with gene expression profiling, for example, to describe describe cis- and trans-controlling elements for the expression of phenotype associated genes."}
{"uri":"operation_3233","label":"Copy number estimation","definition":"Estimate the number of copies of loci of particular gene(s) in DNA sequences typically from gene-expression profiling technology based on microarray hybridisation-based experiments. For example, estimate copy number (or marker dosage) of a dominant marker in samples from polyploid plant cells or tissues, or chromosomal gains and losses in tumors."}
{"uri":"operation_3237","label":"Primer removal","definition":"Remove forward and/or reverse primers from nucleic acid sequences (typically PCR products)."}
{"uri":"operation_3258","label":"Transcriptome assembly","definition":"Infer a transcriptome sequence by analysis of short sequence reads."}
{"uri":"operation_3267","label":"Sequence coordinate conversion","definition":"Convert one set of sequence coordinates to another, e.g. convert coordinates of one assembly to another, cDNA to genomic, CDS to genomic, protein translation to genomic etc."}
{"uri":"operation_3278","label":"Document similarity calculation","definition":"Calculate similarity between 2 or more documents."}
{"uri":"operation_3279","label":"Document clustering","definition":"Cluster (group) documents on the basis of their calculated similarity."}
{"uri":"operation_3280","label":"Named-entity and concept recognition","definition":"Recognise named entities, ontology concepts, tags, events, and dictionary terms within documents."}
{"uri":"operation_3282","label":"ID mapping","definition":"Map data identifiers to one another for example to establish a link between two biological databases for the purposes of data integration."}
{"uri":"operation_3283","label":"Anonymisation","definition":"Process data in such a way that makes it hard to trace to the person which the data concerns."}
{"uri":"operation_3348","label":"Sequence checksum generation","definition":"Generate a checksum of a molecular sequence."}
{"uri":"operation_3349","label":"Bibliography generation","definition":"Construct a bibliography from the scientific literature."}
{"uri":"operation_3350","label":"Protein quaternary structure prediction","definition":"Predict the structure of a multi-subunit protein and particularly how the subunits fit together."}
{"uri":"operation_3351","label":"Molecular surface analysis","definition":"Analyse the surface properties of proteins or other macromolecules, including surface accessible pockets, interior inaccessible cavities etc."}
{"uri":"operation_3352","label":"Ontology comparison","definition":"Compare two or more ontologies, e.g. identify differences."}
{"uri":"operation_3357","label":"Format detection","definition":"Recognition of which format the given data is in."}
{"uri":"operation_3359","label":"Splitting","definition":"Split a file containing multiple data items into many files, each containing one item."}
{"uri":"operation_3429","label":"Generation","definition":"Construct some data entity."}
{"uri":"operation_3431","label":"Data deposition","definition":"Data deposition is the submission and upload of data to a dedicated repository, archive, or deposition database, usually with accompanying metadata."}
{"uri":"operation_3432","label":"Clustering","definition":"Group together some data entities on the basis of similarities such that entities in the same group (cluster) are more similar to each other than to those in other groups (clusters)."}
{"uri":"operation_3434","label":"Conversion","definition":"Convert a data set from one form to another."}
{"uri":"operation_3435","label":"Standardisation and normalisation","definition":"Standardize or normalize data by some statistical method."}
{"uri":"operation_3436","label":"Aggregation","definition":"Combine multiple files or data items into a single file or object."}
{"uri":"operation_3437","label":"Article comparison","definition":"Compare two or more scientific articles."}
{"uri":"operation_3438","label":"Calculation","definition":"Mathematical determination of the value of something, typically a properly of a molecule."}
{"uri":"operation_3443","label":"Image analysis","definition":"The analysis of a image (typically a digital image) of some type in order to extract information from it."}
{"uri":"operation_3445","label":"Diffraction data analysis","definition":"Analysis of data from a diffraction experiment."}
{"uri":"operation_3446","label":"Cell migration analysis","definition":"Analysis of cell migration images in order to study cell migration, typically in order to study the processes that play a role in the disease progression."}
{"uri":"operation_3447","label":"Diffraction data reduction","definition":"Processing of diffraction data into a corrected, ordered, and simplified form."}
{"uri":"operation_3450","label":"Neurite measurement","definition":"Measurement of neurites; projections (axons or dendrites) from the cell body of a neuron, from analysis of neuron images."}
{"uri":"operation_3453","label":"Diffraction data integration","definition":"The evaluation of diffraction intensities and integration of diffraction maxima from a diffraction experiment."}
{"uri":"operation_3454","label":"Phasing","definition":"Phase a macromolecular crystal structure, for example by using molecular replacement or experimental phasing methods."}
{"uri":"operation_3455","label":"Molecular replacement","definition":"A technique used to construct an atomic model of an unknown structure from diffraction data, based upon an atomic model of a known structure, either a related protein or the same protein from a different crystal form."}
{"uri":"operation_3456","label":"Rigid body refinement","definition":"A method used to refine a structure by moving the whole molecule or parts of it as a rigid unit, rather than moving individual atoms."}
{"uri":"operation_3457","label":"Single particle analysis","definition":"An image processing technique that combines and analyze multiple images of a particulate sample, in order to produce an image with clearer features that are more easily interpreted."}
{"uri":"operation_3458","label":"Single particle alignment and classification","definition":"Compare (align and classify) multiple particle images from a micrograph in order to produce a representative image of the particle."}
{"uri":"operation_3459","label":"Functional clustering","definition":"Clustering of molecular sequences on the basis of their function, typically using information from an ontology of gene function, or some other measure of functional phenotype."}
{"uri":"operation_3460","label":"Taxonomic classification","definition":"Classification (typically of molecular sequences) by assignment to some taxonomic hierarchy."}
{"uri":"operation_3461","label":"Virulence prediction","definition":"The prediction of the degree of pathogenicity of a microorganism from analysis of molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_3463","label":"Expression correlation analysis","definition":"Analyse the correlation patterns among features/molecules across across a variety of experiments, samples etc."}
{"uri":"operation_3465","label":"Correlation","definition":"Identify a correlation, i.e. a statistical relationship between two random variables or two sets of data."}
{"uri":"operation_3469","label":"RNA structure covariance model generation","definition":"Compute the covariance model for (a family of) RNA secondary structures."}
{"uri":"operation_3472","label":"k-mer counting","definition":"Count k-mers (substrings of length k) in DNA sequence data."}
{"uri":"operation_3478","label":"Phylogenetic reconstruction","definition":"Reconstructing the inner node labels of a phylogenetic tree from its leafes."}
{"uri":"operation_3480","label":"Probabilistic data generation","definition":"Generate some data from a chosen probibalistic model, possibly to evaluate algorithms."}
{"uri":"operation_3481","label":"Probabilistic sequence generation","definition":"Generate sequences from some probabilistic model, e.g. a model that simulates evolution."}
{"uri":"operation_3482","label":"Antimicrobial resistance prediction","definition":"Identify or predict causes for antibiotic resistance from molecular sequence analysis."}
{"uri":"operation_3501","label":"Enrichment analysis","definition":"Analysis of a set of objects, such as genes, annotated with given categories, where eventual over-/under-representation of certain categories within the studied set of objects is revealed."}
{"uri":"operation_3502","label":"Chemical similarity enrichment","definition":"Analyse a dataset with respect to concepts from an ontology of chemical structure, leveraging chemical similarity information."}
{"uri":"operation_3503","label":"Incident curve plotting","definition":"Plot an incident curve such as a survival curve, death curve, mortality curve."}
{"uri":"operation_3504","label":"Variant pattern analysis","definition":"Identify and map patterns of genomic variations."}
{"uri":"operation_3552","label":"Microscope image visualisation","definition":"Visualise images resulting from various types of microscopy."}
{"uri":"operation_3553","label":"Image annotation","definition":"Annotate an image of some sort, typically with terms from a controlled vocabulary."}
{"uri":"operation_3557","label":"Imputation","definition":"Replace missing data with substituted values, usually by using some statistical or other mathematical approach."}
{"uri":"operation_3559","label":"Ontology visualisation","definition":"Visualise, format or render data from an ontology, typically a tree of terms."}
{"uri":"operation_3560","label":"Maximum occurrence analysis","definition":"A method for making numerical assessments about the maximum percent of time that a conformer of a flexible macromolecule can exist and still be compatible with the experimental data."}
{"uri":"operation_3561","label":"Database comparison","definition":"Compare the models or schemas used by two or more databases, or any other general comparison of databases rather than a detailed comparison of the entries themselves."}
{"uri":"operation_3563","label":"RNA-seq read count analysis","definition":"Analyze read counts from RNA-seq experiments."}
{"uri":"operation_3564","label":"Chemical redundancy removal","definition":"Identify and remove redundancy from a set of small molecule structures."}
{"uri":"operation_3565","label":"RNA-seq time series data analysis","definition":"Analyze time series data from an RNA-seq experiment."}
{"uri":"operation_3566","label":"Simulated gene expression data generation","definition":"Simulate gene expression data, e.g. for purposes of benchmarking."}
{"uri":"operation_3625","label":"Relation extraction","definition":"Identify semantic relations among entities and concepts within a text, using text mining techniques."}
{"uri":"operation_3627","label":"Mass spectra calibration","definition":"Re-adjust the output of mass spectrometry experiments with shifted ppm values."}
{"uri":"operation_3628","label":"Chromatographic alignment","definition":"Align multiple data sets using information from chromatography and/or peptide identification, from mass spectrometry experiments."}
{"uri":"operation_3629","label":"Deisotoping","definition":"The removal of isotope peaks in a spectrum, to represent the fragment ion as one data point."}
{"uri":"operation_3630","label":"Protein quantification","definition":"Technique for determining the amount of proteins in a sample."}
{"uri":"operation_3631","label":"Peptide identification","definition":"Determination of peptide sequence from mass spectrum."}
{"uri":"operation_3632","label":"Isotopic distributions calculation","definition":"Calculate the isotope distribution of a given chemical species."}
{"uri":"operation_3633","label":"Retention time prediction","definition":"Prediction of retention time in a mass spectrometry experiment based on compositional and structural properties of the separated species."}
{"uri":"operation_3634","label":"Label-free quantification","definition":"Quantification without the use of chemical tags."}
{"uri":"operation_3635","label":"Labeled quantification","definition":"Quantification based on the use of chemical tags."}
{"uri":"operation_3636","label":"MRM/SRM","definition":"Quantification by Selected/multiple Reaction Monitoring workflow (XIC quantitation of precursor / fragment mass pair)."}
{"uri":"operation_3637","label":"Spectral counting","definition":"Calculate number of identified MS2 spectra as approximation of peptide / protein quantity."}
{"uri":"operation_3638","label":"SILAC","definition":"Quantification analysis using stable isotope labeling by amino acids in cell culture."}
{"uri":"operation_3639","label":"iTRAQ","definition":"Quantification analysis using the AB SCIEX iTRAQ isobaric labelling workflow, wherein 2-8 reporter ions are measured in MS2 spectra near 114 m/z."}
{"uri":"operation_3640","label":"18O labeling","definition":"Quantification analysis using labeling based on 18O-enriched H2O."}
{"uri":"operation_3641","label":"TMT-tag","definition":"Quantification analysis using the Thermo Fisher tandem mass tag labelling workflow."}
{"uri":"operation_3642","label":"Stable isotope dimethyl labelling","definition":"Quantification analysis using chemical labeling by stable isotope dimethylation."}
{"uri":"operation_3643","label":"Tag-based peptide identification","definition":"Peptide sequence tags are used as piece of information about a peptide obtained by tandem mass spectrometry."}
{"uri":"operation_3644","label":"de Novo sequencing","definition":"Analytical process that derives a peptide's amino acid sequence from its tandem mass spectrum (MS/MS) without the assistance of a sequence database."}
{"uri":"operation_3645","label":"PTM identification","definition":"Identification of post-translational modifications (PTMs) of peptides/proteins in mass spectrum."}
{"uri":"operation_3646","label":"Peptide database search","definition":"Determination of best matches between MS/MS spectrum and a database of protein or nucleic acid sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_3647","label":"Blind peptide database search","definition":"Peptide database search for identification of known and unknown PTMs looking for mass difference mismatches."}
{"uri":"operation_3649","label":"Target-Decoy","definition":"Statistical estimation of false discovery rate from score distribution for peptide-spectrum-matches, following a peptide database search, and by comparison to search results with a database containing incorrect information."}
{"uri":"operation_3658","label":"Statistical inference","definition":"Analyse data in order to deduce properties of an underlying distribution or population."}
{"uri":"operation_3659","label":"Regression analysis","definition":"A statistical calculation to estimate the relationships among variables."}
{"uri":"operation_3660","label":"Metabolic network modelling","definition":"Model a metabolic network. This can include 1) reconstruction to break down a metabolic pathways into reactions, enzymes, and other relevant information, and compilation of this into a mathematical model and 2) simulations of metabolism based on the model."}
{"uri":"operation_3661","label":"SNP annotation","definition":"Predict the effect or function of an individual single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP)."}
{"uri":"operation_3662","label":"Ab-initio gene prediction","definition":"Prediction of genes or gene components from first principles, i.e. without reference to existing genes."}
{"uri":"operation_3663","label":"Homology-based gene prediction","definition":"Prediction of genes or gene components by reference to homologous genes."}
{"uri":"operation_3664","label":"Statistical modelling","definition":"Construction of a statistical model, or a set of assumptions around some observed data, usually by describing a set of probability distributions which approximate the distribution of data."}
{"uri":"operation_3666","label":"Molecular surface comparison","definition":"Compare two or more molecular surfaces."}
{"uri":"operation_3672","label":"Gene functional annotation","definition":"Annotate one or more sequences with functional information, such as cellular processes or metaobolic pathways, by reference to a controlled vocabulary - invariably the Gene Ontology (GO)."}
{"uri":"operation_3675","label":"Variant filtering","definition":"Variant filtering is used to eliminate false positive variants based for example on base calling quality, strand and position information, and mapping info."}
{"uri":"operation_3677","label":"Differential binding analysis","definition":"Identify binding sites in nucleic acid sequences that are statistically significantly differentially bound between sample groups."}
{"uri":"operation_3680","label":"RNA-Seq analysis","definition":"Analyze data from RNA-seq experiments."}
{"uri":"operation_3694","label":"Mass spectrum visualisation","definition":"Visualise, format or render a mass spectrum."}
{"uri":"operation_3695","label":"Data filtering","definition":"Filter a set of files or data items according to some property."}
{"uri":"operation_3703","label":"Reference identification","definition":"Identification of the best reference for mapping for a specific dataset from a list of potential references, when performing genetic variation analysis."}
{"uri":"operation_3704","label":"Ion counting","definition":"Label-free quantification by integration of ion current (ion counting)."}
{"uri":"operation_3705","label":"Isotope-coded protein label","definition":"Chemical tagging free amino groups of intact proteins with stable isotopes."}
{"uri":"operation_3715","label":"Metabolic labeling","definition":"Labeling all proteins and (possibly) all amino acids using C-13 or N-15 enriched grown medium or feed."}
{"uri":"operation_3730","label":"Cross-assembly","definition":"Construction of a single sequence assembly of all reads from different samples, typically as part of a comparative metagenomic analysis."}
{"uri":"operation_3731","label":"Sample comparison","definition":"The comparison of samples from a metagenomics study, for example, by comparison of metagenome shotgun reads or assembled contig sequences, by comparison of functional profiles, or some other method."}
{"uri":"operation_3741","label":"Differential protein expression profiling","definition":"The analysis, using proteomics techniques, to identify proteins whose encoding genes are differentially expressed under a given experimental setup."}
{"uri":"operation_3744","label":"Multiple sample visualisation","definition":"Visualise, format or render data arising from an analysis of multiple samples from a metagenomics/community experiment."}
{"uri":"operation_3745","label":"Ancestral reconstruction","definition":"The extrapolation of empirical characteristics of individuals or populations, backwards in time, to their common ancestors."}
{"uri":"operation_3755","label":"PTM localisation","definition":"Site localisation of post-translational modifications in peptide or protein mass spectra."}
{"uri":"operation_3760","label":"Service management","definition":"Operations concerning the handling and use of other tools."}
{"uri":"operation_3761","label":"Service discovery","definition":"An operation supporting the browsing or discovery of other tools and services."}
{"uri":"operation_3762","label":"Service composition","definition":"An operation supporting the aggregation of other services (at least two) into a functional unit, for the automation of some task."}
{"uri":"operation_3763","label":"Service invocation","definition":"An operation supporting the calling (invocation) of other tools and services."}
{"uri":"operation_3766","label":"Weighted correlation network analysis","definition":"A data mining method typically used for studying biological networks based on pairwise correlations between variables."}
{"uri":"operation_3767","label":"Protein identification","definition":"Identification of protein, for example from one or more peptide identifications by tandem mass spectrometry."}
{"uri":"operation_3778","label":"Text annotation","definition":"Text annotation is the operation of adding notes, data and metadata, recognised entities and concepts, and their relations to a text (such as a scientific article)."}
{"uri":"operation_3791","label":"Collapsing methods","definition":"A method whereby data on several variants are \"collapsed\" into a single covariate based on regions such as genes."}
{"uri":"operation_3792","label":"miRNA expression analysis","definition":"The analysis of microRNAs (miRNAs) : short, highly conserved small noncoding RNA molecules that are naturally occurring plant and animal genomes."}
{"uri":"operation_3793","label":"Read summarisation","definition":"Counting and summarising the number of short sequence reads that map to genomic features."}
{"uri":"operation_3795","label":"In vitro selection","definition":"A technique whereby molecules with desired properties and function are isolated from libraries of random molecules, through iterative cycles of selection, amplification, and mutagenesis."}
{"uri":"operation_3797","label":"Rarefaction","definition":"The calculation of species richness for a number of individual samples, based on plots of the number of species as a function of the number of samples (rarefaction curves)."}
{"uri":"operation_3798","label":"Read binning","definition":"An operation which groups reads or contigs and assigns them to operational taxonomic units."}
{"uri":"operation_3799","label":"Quantification","definition":"Counting and measuring experimentally determined observations into quantities."}
{"uri":"operation_3800","label":"RNA-Seq quantification","definition":"Quantification of data arising from RNA-Seq high-throughput sequencing, typically the quantification of transcript abundances durnig transcriptome analysis in a gene expression study."}
{"uri":"operation_3801","label":"Spectral library search","definition":"Match experimentally measured mass spectrum to a spectrum in a spectral library or database."}
{"uri":"operation_3802","label":"Data sorting","definition":"Sort a set of files or data items according to some property."}
{"uri":"operation_3803","label":"Natural product identification","definition":"Mass spectra identification of compounds that are produced by living systems. Including polyketides, terpenoids, phenylpropanoids, alkaloids and antibiotics."}
{"uri":"operation_3809","label":"DMR identification","definition":"Identify and assess specific genes or regulatory regions of interest that are differentially methylated."}
{"uri":"operation_3840","label":"Multilocus sequence typing","definition":"Genotyping of multiple loci, typically characterizing microbial species isolates using internal fragments of multiple housekeeping genes."}
{"uri":"operation_3860","label":"Spectrum calculation","definition":"Calculate a theoretical mass spectrometry spectra for given sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_3890","label":"Trajectory visualization","definition":"3D visualization of a molecular trajectory."}
{"uri":"operation_3891","label":"Essential dynamics","definition":"Compute Essential Dynamics (ED) on a simulation trajectory: an analysis of molecule dynamics using PCA (Principal Component Analysis) applied to the atomic positional fluctuations."}
{"uri":"operation_3893","label":"Forcefield parameterisation","definition":"Obtain force field parameters (charge, bonds, dihedrals, etc.) from a molecule, to be used in molecular simulations."}
{"uri":"operation_3894","label":"DNA profiling","definition":"Analyse DNA sequences in order to determine an individual's DNA characteristics, for example in criminal forensics, parentage testing and so on."}
{"uri":"operation_3896","label":"Active site prediction","definition":"Predict or detect active sites in proteins; the region of an enzyme which binds a substrate bind and catalyses a reaction."}
{"uri":"operation_3897","label":"Ligand-binding site prediction","definition":"Predict or detect ligand-binding sites in proteins; a region of a protein which reversibly binds a ligand for some biochemical purpose, such as transport or regulation of protein function."}
{"uri":"operation_3898","label":"Metal-binding site prediction","definition":"Predict or detect metal ion-binding sites in proteins."}
{"uri":"operation_3899","label":"Protein-protein docking","definition":"Model or simulate protein-protein binding using comparative modelling or other techniques."}
{"uri":"operation_3900","label":"DNA-binding protein prediction","definition":"Predict DNA-binding proteins."}
{"uri":"operation_3901","label":"RNA-binding protein prediction","definition":"Predict RNA-binding proteins."}
{"uri":"operation_3902","label":"RNA binding site prediction","definition":"Predict or detect RNA-binding sites in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_3903","label":"DNA binding site prediction","definition":"Predict or detect DNA-binding sites in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_3904","label":"Protein disorder prediction","definition":"Identify or predict intrinsically disordered regions in proteins."}
{"uri":"operation_3907","label":"Information extraction","definition":"Extract structured information from unstructured (\"free\") or semi-structured textual documents."}
{"uri":"operation_3908","label":"Information retrieval","definition":"Retrieve resources from information systems matching a specific information need."}
{"uri":"operation_3918","label":"Genome analysis","definition":"Study of genomic feature structure, variation, function and evolution at a genomic scale."}
{"uri":"operation_3919","label":"Methylation calling","definition":"The determination of cytosine methylation status of specific positions in a nucleic acid sequences (usually reads from a bisulfite sequencing experiment)."}
{"uri":"operation_3920","label":"DNA testing","definition":"The identification of changes in DNA sequence or chromosome structure, usually in the context of diagnostic tests for disease, or to study ancestry or phylogeny."}
{"uri":"operation_3921","label":"Sequence read processing","definition":"The processing of reads from high-throughput sequencing machines."}
{"uri":"operation_3925","label":"Network visualisation","definition":"Render (visualise) a network - typically a biological network of some sort."}
{"uri":"operation_3926","label":"Pathway visualisation","definition":"Render (visualise) a biological pathway."}
{"uri":"operation_3927","label":"Network analysis","definition":"Generate, process or analyse a biological network."}
{"uri":"operation_3928","label":"Pathway analysis","definition":"Generate, process or analyse a biological pathway."}
{"uri":"operation_3929","label":"Metabolic pathway prediction","definition":"Predict a metabolic pathway."}
{"uri":"operation_3933","label":"Demultiplexing","definition":"Assigning sequence reads to separate groups / files based on their index tag (sample origin)."}
{"uri":"operation_3935","label":"Dimensionality reduction","definition":"A process used in statistics, machine learning, and information theory that reduces the number of random variables by obtaining a set of principal variables."}
{"uri":"operation_3936","label":"Feature selection","definition":"A dimensionality reduction process that selects a subset of relevant features (variables, predictors) for use in model construction."}
{"uri":"operation_3937","label":"Feature extraction","definition":"A dimensionality reduction process which builds (ideally) informative and non-redundant values (features) from an initial set of measured data, to aid subsequent generalization, learning or interpretation."}
{"uri":"operation_3938","label":"Virtual screening","definition":"Virtual screening is used in drug discovery to identify potential drug compounds. It involves searching libraries of small molecules in order to identify those molecules which are most likely to bind to a drug target (typically a protein receptor or enzyme)."}
{"uri":"operation_3942","label":"Tree dating","definition":"The application of phylogenetic and other methods to estimate paleogeographical events such as speciation."}
{"uri":"operation_3946","label":"Ecological modelling","definition":"The development and use of mathematical models and systems analysis for the description of ecological processes, and applications such as the sustainable management of resources."}
{"uri":"operation_3947","label":"Phylogenetic tree reconciliation","definition":"Mapping between gene tree nodes and species tree nodes or branches, to analyse and account for possible differences between gene histories and species histories, explaining this in terms of gene-scale events such as duplication, loss, transfer etc."}
{"uri":"operation_3950","label":"Selection detection","definition":"The detection of genetic selection, or (the end result of) the process by which certain traits become more prevalent in a species than other traits."}
{"uri":"operation_3960","label":"Principal component analysis","definition":"A statistical procedure that uses an orthogonal transformation to convert a set of observations of possibly correlated variables into a set of values of linearly uncorrelated variables called principal components."}
{"uri":"operation_3961","label":"Copy number variation detection","definition":"Identify where sections of the genome are repeated and the number of repeats in the genome varies between individuals."}
{"uri":"operation_3962","label":"Deletion detection","definition":"Identify deletion events causing the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals."}
{"uri":"operation_3963","label":"Duplication detection","definition":"Identify duplication events causing the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals."}
{"uri":"operation_3964","label":"Complex CNV detection","definition":"Identify copy number variations which are complex, e.g. multi-allelic variations that have many structural alleles and have rearranged multiple times in the ancestral genomes."}
{"uri":"operation_3965","label":"Amplification detection","definition":"Identify amplification events causing the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals."}
{"uri":"operation_3968","label":"Adhesin prediction","definition":"Predict adhesins in protein sequences."}
{"uri":"operation_4008","label":"Protein design","definition":"Design new protein molecules with specific structural or functional properties."}
{"uri":"operation_4009","label":"Small molecule design","definition":"The design of small molecules with specific biological activity, such as inhibitors or modulators for proteins that are of therapeutic interest. This can involve the modification of individual atoms, the addition or removal of molecular fragments, and the use reaction-based design to explore tractable synthesis options for the small molecule."}
{"uri":"operation_4031","label":"Power test","definition":"The estimation of the power of a test; that is the probability of correctly rejecting the null hypothesis when it is false."}
{"uri":"operation_4032","label":"DNA modification prediction","definition":"The prediction of DNA modifications (e.g. N4-methylcytosine and N6-Methyladenine) using, for example, statistical models."}
{"uri":"operation_4033","label":"Disease transmission analysis","definition":"The analysis and simulation of disease transmission using, for example, statistical methods such as the SIR-model."}
{"uri":"operation_4034","label":"Multiple testing correction","definition":"The correction of p-values from multiple statistical tests to correct for false positives."}
{"uri":"operation_4042","label":"Data management planning","definition":"Data management planning is the process of creating and updating a data management plan (DMP) for a project or an organisation."}
{"uri":"operation_4043","label":"Data digitisation","definition":"Data digitisation is the process of converting analog data, text, or information into a digital format, appropriate for computational analysis and preservation."}
{"uri":"operation_4074","label":"Compound identification","definition":"Compound identification is the process of determining the chemical identity of compounds detected in analytical experiments such as mass spectrometry or NMR spectroscopy. Identification is typically achieved by matching experimental spectral or physicochemical features against reference databases, spectral libraries, or predicted molecular properties."}
{"uri":"topic_0003","label":"Topic","definition":"A category denoting a rather broad domain or field of interest, of study, application, work, data, or technology. Topics have no clearly defined borders between each other."}
{"uri":"topic_0077","label":"Nucleic acids","definition":"The processing and analysis of nucleic acid sequence, structural and other data."}
{"uri":"topic_0078","label":"Proteins","definition":"Archival, processing and analysis of protein data, typically molecular sequence and structural data."}
{"uri":"topic_0080","label":"Sequence analysis","definition":"The archival, processing and analysis of molecular sequences (monomer composition of polymers) including molecular sequence data resources, sequence sites, alignments, motifs and profiles."}
{"uri":"topic_0081","label":"Structure analysis","definition":"The curation, processing, analysis and prediction of data about the structure of biological molecules, typically proteins and nucleic acids and other macromolecules."}
{"uri":"topic_0082","label":"Structure prediction","definition":"The prediction of molecular structure, including the prediction, modelling, recognition or design of protein secondary or tertiary structure or other structural features, and the folding of nucleic acid molecules and the prediction or design of nucleic acid (typically RNA) sequences with specific conformations."}
{"uri":"topic_0084","label":"Phylogeny","definition":"The study of evolutionary relationships amongst organisms."}
{"uri":"topic_0085","label":"Functional genomics","definition":"The study of gene or protein functions and their interactions in totality in a given organism, tissue, cell etc."}
{"uri":"topic_0089","label":"Ontology and terminology","definition":"The conceptualisation, categorisation and nomenclature (naming) of entities or phenomena within biology or bioinformatics. This includes formal ontologies, controlled vocabularies, structured glossary, symbols and terminology or other related resource."}
{"uri":"topic_0091","label":"Bioinformatics","definition":"The archival, curation, processing and analysis of complex biological data."}
{"uri":"topic_0092","label":"Data visualisation","definition":"Rendering (drawing on a computer screen) or visualisation of molecular sequences, structures or other biomolecular data."}
{"uri":"topic_0097","label":"Nucleic acid structure analysis","definition":"The archival, curation, processing and analysis of nucleic acid structural information, such as whole structures, structural features and alignments, and associated annotation."}
{"uri":"topic_0099","label":"RNA","definition":"RNA sequences and structures."}
{"uri":"topic_0102","label":"Mapping","definition":"The mapping of complete (typically nucleotide) sequences. Mapping (in the sense of short read alignment, or more generally, just alignment) has application in RNA-Seq analysis (mapping of transcriptomics reads), variant discovery (e.g. mapping of exome capture), and re-sequencing (mapping of WGS reads)."}
{"uri":"topic_0108","label":"Protein expression","definition":"The translation of mRNA into protein and subsequent protein processing in the cell."}
{"uri":"topic_0114","label":"Gene structure","definition":"Gene structure, regions which make an RNA product and features such as promoters, coding regions, gene fusion, splice sites etc."}
{"uri":"topic_0121","label":"Proteomics","definition":"Proteomics is in the narrow sense (sensu stricto) the application of methods to separate, characterise, identify, and quantify all proteins (the proteome) - or a substantial set of proteins - that are present in a sample. Proteomics in the broad sense is the science of proteins and peptides on the large scale."}
{"uri":"topic_0122","label":"Structural genomics","definition":"The elucidation of the three dimensional structure for all (available) proteins in a given organism."}
{"uri":"topic_0123","label":"Protein properties","definition":"The study of the physical and biochemical properties of peptides and proteins, for example the hydrophobic, hydrophilic and charge properties of a protein."}
{"uri":"topic_0128","label":"Protein interactions","definition":"Protein-protein, protein-DNA/RNA and protein-ligand interactions, including analysis of known interactions and prediction of putative interactions."}
{"uri":"topic_0130","label":"Protein folding, stability and design","definition":"Protein stability, folding (in 3D space) and protein sequence-structure-function relationships. This includes for example study of inter-atomic or inter-residue interactions in protein (3D) structures, the effect of mutation, and the design of proteins with specific properties, typically by designing changes (via site-directed mutagenesis) to an existing protein."}
{"uri":"topic_0140","label":"Protein targeting and localisation","definition":"The study of how proteins are transported within and without the cell, including signal peptides, protein subcellular localisation and export."}
{"uri":"topic_0152","label":"Carbohydrates","definition":"Carbohydrates, typically including structural information."}
{"uri":"topic_0153","label":"Lipidomics","definition":"Lipids and their structures."}
{"uri":"topic_0154","label":"Small molecules","definition":"Small molecules of biological significance, typically archival, curation, processing and analysis of structural information."}
{"uri":"topic_0157","label":"Sequence composition, complexity and repeats","definition":"The archival, processing and analysis of the basic character composition of molecular sequences, for example character or word frequency, ambiguity, complexity, particularly regions of low complexity, and repeats or the repetitive nature of molecular sequences."}
{"uri":"topic_0160","label":"Sequence sites, features and motifs","definition":"The archival, detection, prediction and analysis of positional features such as functional and other key sites, in molecular sequences and the conserved patterns (motifs, profiles etc.) that may be used to describe them."}
{"uri":"topic_0166","label":"Protein structural motifs and surfaces","definition":"Structural features or common 3D motifs within protein structures, including the surface of a protein structure, such as biological interfaces with other molecules."}
{"uri":"topic_0176","label":"Molecular dynamics","definition":"The study and simulation of molecular (typically protein) conformation using a computational model of physical forces and computer simulation."}
{"uri":"topic_0194","label":"Phylogenomics","definition":"The integrated study of evolutionary relationships and whole genome data, for example, in the analysis of species trees, horizontal gene transfer and evolutionary reconstruction."}
{"uri":"topic_0196","label":"Sequence assembly","definition":"The assembly of fragments of a DNA sequence to reconstruct the original sequence."}
{"uri":"topic_0199","label":"Genetic variation","definition":"Stable, naturally occurring mutations in a nucleotide sequence including alleles, naturally occurring mutations such as single base nucleotide substitutions, deletions and insertions, RFLPs and other polymorphisms."}
{"uri":"topic_0202","label":"Pharmacology","definition":"The study of drugs and their effects or responses in living systems."}
{"uri":"topic_0203","label":"Gene expression","definition":"The analysis of levels and patterns of synthesis of gene products (proteins and functional RNA) including interpretation in functional terms of gene expression data."}
{"uri":"topic_0204","label":"Gene regulation","definition":"The regulation of gene expression."}
{"uri":"topic_0208","label":"Pharmacogenomics","definition":"The influence of genotype on drug response, for example by correlating gene expression or single-nucleotide polymorphisms with drug efficacy or toxicity."}
{"uri":"topic_0209","label":"Medicinal chemistry","definition":"The design and chemical synthesis of bioactive molecules, for example drugs or potential drug compounds, for medicinal purposes."}
{"uri":"topic_0218","label":"Natural language processing","definition":"The processing and analysis of natural language, such as scientific literature in English, in order to extract data and information, or to enable human-computer interaction."}
{"uri":"topic_0219","label":"Data curation and archival","definition":"Data curation and archival includes the preservation of data in a repository, archive, or a deposition database; and curation of data and metadata, database accessions, annotation, and data provenance."}
{"uri":"topic_0593","label":"NMR","definition":"An analytical technique that exploits the magenetic properties of certain atomic nuclei to provide information on the structure, dynamics, reaction state and chemical environment of molecules."}
{"uri":"topic_0601","label":"Protein modifications","definition":"Protein chemical modifications, e.g. post-translational modifications."}
{"uri":"topic_0602","label":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","definition":"Molecular interactions, biological pathways, networks and other models."}
{"uri":"topic_0605","label":"Informatics","definition":"The study and practice of information processing and use of computer information systems."}
{"uri":"topic_0607","label":"Laboratory information management","definition":"Laboratory management and resources, for example, catalogues of biological resources for use in the lab including cell lines, viruses, plasmids, phages, DNA probes and primers and so on."}
{"uri":"topic_0610","label":"Ecology","definition":"The ecological and environmental sciences and especially the application of information technology (ecoinformatics)."}
{"uri":"topic_0611","label":"Electron microscopy","definition":"The study of matter by studying the interference pattern from firing electrons at a sample, to analyse structures at resolutions higher than can be achieved using light."}
{"uri":"topic_0621","label":"Model organisms","definition":"A specific organism, or group of organisms, used to study a particular aspect of biology."}
{"uri":"topic_0622","label":"Genomics","definition":"Whole genomes of one or more organisms, or genomes in general, such as meta-information on genomes, genome projects, gene names etc."}
{"uri":"topic_0623","label":"Gene and protein families","definition":"Particular gene(s), gene family or other gene group or system and their encoded proteins.Primarily the classification of proteins (from sequence or structural data) into clusters, groups, families etc., curation of a particular protein or protein family, or any other proteins that have been classified as members of a common group."}
{"uri":"topic_0625","label":"Genotype and phenotype","definition":"The study of genetic constitution of a living entity, such as an individual, and organism, a cell and so on, typically with respect to a particular observable phenotypic traits, or resources concerning such traits, which might be an aspect of biochemistry, physiology, morphology, anatomy, development and so on."}
{"uri":"topic_0632","label":"Probes and primers","definition":"Molecular probes (e.g. a peptide probe or DNA microarray probe) or PCR primers and hybridisation oligos in a nucleic acid sequence."}
{"uri":"topic_0634","label":"Pathology","definition":"Diseases, including diseases in general and the genes, gene variations and proteins involved in one or more specific diseases."}
{"uri":"topic_0637","label":"Taxonomy","definition":"Organism classification, identification and naming."}
{"uri":"topic_0654","label":"DNA","definition":"DNA sequences and structure, including processes such as methylation and replication."}
{"uri":"topic_0659","label":"Functional, regulatory and non-coding RNA","definition":"Non-coding or functional RNA sequences, including regulatory RNA sequences, ribosomal RNA (rRNA) and transfer RNA (tRNA)."}
{"uri":"topic_0736","label":"Protein folds and structural domains","definition":"Protein tertiary structural domains and folds in a protein or polypeptide chain."}
{"uri":"topic_0749","label":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","definition":"Proteins that bind to DNA and control transcription of DNA to mRNA (transcription factors) and also transcriptional regulatory sites, elements and regions (such as promoters, enhancers, silencers and boundary elements / insulators) in nucleotide sequences."}
{"uri":"topic_0769","label":"Workflows","definition":"Biological or biomedical analytical workflows or pipelines."}
{"uri":"topic_0780","label":"Plant biology","definition":"Plants, e.g. information on a specific plant genome including molecular sequences, genes and annotation."}
{"uri":"topic_0781","label":"Virology","definition":"Study of viruses, e.g. sequence and structural data, interactions of viral proteins, or a viral genome including molecular sequences, genes and annotation."}
{"uri":"topic_0797","label":"Comparative genomics","definition":"The study (typically comparison) of the sequence, structure or function of multiple genomes."}
{"uri":"topic_0798","label":"Mobile genetic elements","definition":"Mobile genetic elements, such as transposons, Plasmids, Bacteriophage elements and Group II introns."}
{"uri":"topic_0804","label":"Immunology","definition":"The application of information technology to immunology such as immunological processes, immunological genes, proteins and peptide ligands, antigens and so on."}
{"uri":"topic_0820","label":"Membrane and lipoproteins","definition":"Lipoproteins (protein-lipid assemblies), and proteins or region of a protein that spans or are associated with a membrane."}
{"uri":"topic_0821","label":"Enzymes","definition":"Proteins that catalyze chemical reaction, the kinetics of enzyme-catalysed reactions, enzyme nomenclature etc."}
{"uri":"topic_1317","label":"Structural biology","definition":"The molecular structure of biological molecules, particularly macromolecules such as proteins and nucleic acids."}
{"uri":"topic_1775","label":"Function analysis","definition":"The study of gene and protein function including the prediction of functional properties of a protein."}
{"uri":"topic_2229","label":"Cell biology","definition":"Cells, such as key genes and proteins involved in the cell cycle."}
{"uri":"topic_2258","label":"Cheminformatics","definition":"The application of information technology to chemistry in biological research environment."}
{"uri":"topic_2259","label":"Systems biology","definition":"The holistic modelling and analysis of complex biological systems and the interactions therein."}
{"uri":"topic_2269","label":"Statistics and probability","definition":"The application of statistical methods to biological problems."}
{"uri":"topic_2275","label":"Molecular modelling","definition":"The construction, analysis, evaluation, refinement etc. of models of a molecules properties or behaviour, including the modelling the structure of proteins in complex with small molecules or other macromolecules (docking)."}
{"uri":"topic_2533","label":"DNA mutation","definition":"DNA mutation."}
{"uri":"topic_2640","label":"Oncology","definition":"The study of cancer, for example, genes and proteins implicated in cancer."}
{"uri":"topic_2814","label":"Protein structure analysis","definition":"Protein secondary or tertiary structural data and/or associated annotation."}
{"uri":"topic_2815","label":"Human biology","definition":"The study of human beings in general, including the human genome and proteome."}
{"uri":"topic_2828","label":"X-ray diffraction","definition":"The study of matter and their structure by means of the diffraction of X-rays, typically the diffraction pattern caused by the regularly spaced atoms of a crystalline sample."}
{"uri":"topic_2830","label":"Immunoproteins and antigens","definition":"Immunity-related proteins and their ligands."}
{"uri":"topic_2840","label":"Toxicology","definition":"Toxins and the adverse effects of these chemical substances on living organisms."}
{"uri":"topic_2885","label":"DNA polymorphism","definition":"DNA polymorphism."}
{"uri":"topic_3047","label":"Molecular biology","definition":"The molecular basis of biological activity, particularly the macromolecules (e.g. proteins and nucleic acids) that are essential to life."}
{"uri":"topic_3050","label":"Biodiversity","definition":"The degree of variation of life forms within a given ecosystem, biome or an entire planet."}
{"uri":"topic_3053","label":"Genetics","definition":"The study of genes, genetic variation and heredity in living organisms."}
{"uri":"topic_3055","label":"Quantitative genetics","definition":"The genes and genetic mechanisms such as Mendelian inheritance that underly continuous phenotypic traits (such as height or weight)."}
{"uri":"topic_3056","label":"Population genetics","definition":"The distribution of allele frequencies in a population of organisms and its change subject to evolutionary processes including natural selection, genetic drift, mutation and gene flow."}
{"uri":"topic_3063","label":"Medical informatics","definition":"The application of information technology to health, disease and biomedicine."}
{"uri":"topic_3064","label":"Developmental biology","definition":"How organisms grow and develop."}
{"uri":"topic_3065","label":"Embryology","definition":"The development of organisms between the one-cell stage (typically the zygote) and the end of the embryonic stage."}
{"uri":"topic_3067","label":"Anatomy","definition":"The form and function of the structures of living organisms."}
{"uri":"topic_3068","label":"Literature and language","definition":"The scientific literature, language processing, reference information, and documentation."}
{"uri":"topic_3070","label":"Biology","definition":"The study of life and living organisms, including their morphology, biochemistry, physiology, development, evolution, and so on."}
{"uri":"topic_3071","label":"Data management","definition":"Data management comprises the practices and principles of taking care of data, other than analysing them. This includes for example taking care of the associated metadata, data formats, storage, preservation/archiving, access, and legal aspects related to using and sharing data."}
{"uri":"topic_3077","label":"Data acquisition","definition":"The acquisition of data, typically measurements of physical systems using any type of sampling system, or by another other means."}
{"uri":"topic_3120","label":"Protein variants","definition":"Protein sequence variants produced e.g. from alternative splicing, alternative promoter usage, alternative initiation and ribosomal frameshifting."}
{"uri":"topic_3125","label":"DNA binding sites","definition":"Nucleic acids binding to some other molecule."}
{"uri":"topic_3127","label":"DNA replication and recombination","definition":"DNA replication or recombination."}
{"uri":"topic_3168","label":"Sequencing","definition":"The determination of complete (typically nucleotide) sequences, including those of genomes (full genome sequencing, de novo sequencing and resequencing), amplicons and transcriptomes."}
{"uri":"topic_3169","label":"ChIP-seq","definition":"The analysis of protein-DNA interactions where chromatin immunoprecipitation (ChIP) is used in combination with massively parallel DNA sequencing to identify the binding sites of DNA-associated proteins."}
{"uri":"topic_3170","label":"RNA-Seq","definition":"A topic concerning high-throughput sequencing of cDNA to measure the RNA content (transcriptome) of a sample, for example, to investigate how different alleles of a gene are expressed, detect post-transcriptional mutations or identify gene fusions."}
{"uri":"topic_3172","label":"Metabolomics","definition":"The systematic study of metabolites, the chemical processes they are involved, and the chemical fingerprints of specific cellular processes in a whole cell, tissue, organ or organism."}
{"uri":"topic_3173","label":"Epigenomics","definition":"The study of the epigenetic modifications of a whole cell, tissue, organism etc."}
{"uri":"topic_3174","label":"Metagenomics","definition":"The study of genetic material recovered from environmental samples, and associated environmental data."}
{"uri":"topic_3175","label":"Structural variation","definition":"Variation in chromosome structure including microscopic and submicroscopic types of variation such as deletions, duplications, copy-number variants, insertions, inversions and translocations."}
{"uri":"topic_3176","label":"DNA packaging","definition":"DNA-histone complexes (chromatin), organisation of chromatin into nucleosomes and packaging into higher-order structures."}
{"uri":"topic_3179","label":"ChIP-on-chip","definition":"Experimental techniques that combine chromatin immunoprecipitation ('ChIP') with microarray ('chip'). ChIP-on-chip is used for high-throughput study protein-DNA interactions."}
{"uri":"topic_3277","label":"Sample collections","definition":"Biological samples and specimens."}
{"uri":"topic_3292","label":"Biochemistry","definition":"Chemical substances and physico-chemical processes and that occur within living organisms."}
{"uri":"topic_3293","label":"Phylogenetics","definition":"The study of evolutionary relationships amongst organisms from analysis of genetic information (typically gene or protein sequences)."}
{"uri":"topic_3295","label":"Epigenetics","definition":"Topic concerning the study of heritable changes, for example in gene expression or phenotype, caused by mechanisms other than changes in the DNA sequence."}
{"uri":"topic_3297","label":"Biotechnology","definition":"The exploitation of biological process, structure and function for industrial purposes, for example the genetic manipulation of microorganisms for the antibody production."}
{"uri":"topic_3298","label":"Phenomics","definition":"Phenomes, or the study of the change in phenotype (the physical and biochemical traits of organisms) in response to genetic and environmental factors."}
{"uri":"topic_3299","label":"Evolutionary biology","definition":"The evolutionary processes, from the genetic to environmental scale, that produced life in all its diversity."}
{"uri":"topic_3300","label":"Physiology","definition":"The functions of living organisms and their constituent parts."}
{"uri":"topic_3301","label":"Microbiology","definition":"The biology of microorganisms."}
{"uri":"topic_3302","label":"Parasitology","definition":"The biology of parasites."}
{"uri":"topic_3303","label":"Medicine","definition":"Research in support of healing by diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of disease."}
{"uri":"topic_3304","label":"Neurobiology","definition":"The study of the nervous system and brain; its anatomy, physiology and function."}
{"uri":"topic_3305","label":"Public health and epidemiology","definition":"Topic concerning the the patterns, cause, and effect of disease within populations."}
{"uri":"topic_3306","label":"Biophysics","definition":"The use of physics to study biological system."}
{"uri":"topic_3307","label":"Computational biology","definition":"The development and application of theory, analytical methods, mathematical models and computational simulation of biological systems."}
{"uri":"topic_3308","label":"Transcriptomics","definition":"The analysis of transcriptomes, or a set of all the RNA molecules in a specific cell, tissue etc."}
{"uri":"topic_3314","label":"Chemistry","definition":"The composition and properties of matter, reactions, and the use of reactions to create new substances."}
{"uri":"topic_3315","label":"Mathematics","definition":"The study of numbers (quantity) and other topics including structure, space, and change."}
{"uri":"topic_3316","label":"Computer science","definition":"The theory and practical use of computer systems."}
{"uri":"topic_3318","label":"Physics","definition":"The study of matter, space and time, and related concepts such as energy and force."}
{"uri":"topic_3320","label":"RNA splicing","definition":"RNA splicing; post-transcription RNA modification involving the removal of introns and joining of exons."}
{"uri":"topic_3321","label":"Molecular genetics","definition":"The structure and function of genes at a molecular level."}
{"uri":"topic_3322","label":"Respiratory medicine","definition":"The study of respiratory system."}
{"uri":"topic_3324","label":"Infectious disease","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the prevention, diagnosis and management of transmissible disease with clinically evident illness resulting from infection with pathogenic biological agents (viruses, bacteria, fungi, protozoa, parasites and prions)."}
{"uri":"topic_3325","label":"Rare diseases","definition":"The study of rare diseases."}
{"uri":"topic_3332","label":"Computational chemistry","definition":"Topic concerning the development and application of theory, analytical methods, mathematical models and computational simulation of chemical systems."}
{"uri":"topic_3334","label":"Neurology","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the anatomy, functions and disorders of the nervous system."}
{"uri":"topic_3335","label":"Cardiology","definition":"The diseases and abnormalities of the heart and circulatory system."}
{"uri":"topic_3336","label":"Drug discovery","definition":"The discovery and design of drugs or potential drug compounds."}
{"uri":"topic_3337","label":"Biobank","definition":"Repositories of biological samples, typically human, for basic biological and clinical research."}
{"uri":"topic_3338","label":"Mouse clinic","definition":"Laboratory study of mice, for example, phenotyping, and mutagenesis of mouse cell lines."}
{"uri":"topic_3339","label":"Microbial collection","definition":"Collections of microbial cells including bacteria, yeasts and moulds."}
{"uri":"topic_3340","label":"Cell culture collection","definition":"Collections of cells grown under laboratory conditions, specifically, cells from multi-cellular eukaryotes and especially animal cells."}
{"uri":"topic_3341","label":"Clone library","definition":"Collections of DNA, including both collections of cloned molecules, and populations of micro-organisms that store and propagate cloned DNA."}
{"uri":"topic_3342","label":"Translational medicine","definition":"'translating' the output of basic and biomedical research into better diagnostic tools, medicines, medical procedures, policies and advice."}
{"uri":"topic_3343","label":"Compound libraries and screening","definition":"Collections of chemicals, typically for use in high-throughput screening experiments."}
{"uri":"topic_3344","label":"Biomedical science","definition":"Topic concerning biological science that is (typically) performed in the context of medicine."}
{"uri":"topic_3345","label":"Data identity and mapping","definition":"Topic concerning the identity of biological entities, or reports on such entities, and the mapping of entities and records in different databases."}
{"uri":"topic_3360","label":"Biomarkers","definition":"Objective indicators of biological state often used to assess health, and determinate treatment."}
{"uri":"topic_3365","label":"Data architecture, analysis and design","definition":"The development of policies, models and standards that cover data acquisition, storage and integration, such that it can be put to use, typically through a process of systematically applying statistical and / or logical techniques to describe, illustrate, summarise or evaluate data."}
{"uri":"topic_3366","label":"Data integration and warehousing","definition":"The combination and integration of data from different sources, for example into a central repository or warehouse, to provide users with a unified view of these data."}
{"uri":"topic_3368","label":"Biomaterials","definition":"Any matter, surface or construct that interacts with a biological system."}
{"uri":"topic_3369","label":"Chemical biology","definition":"The use of synthetic chemistry to study and manipulate biological systems."}
{"uri":"topic_3370","label":"Analytical chemistry","definition":"The study of the separation, identification, and quantification of the chemical components of natural and artificial materials."}
{"uri":"topic_3371","label":"Synthetic chemistry","definition":"The use of chemistry to create new compounds."}
{"uri":"topic_3372","label":"Software engineering","definition":"The process that leads from an original formulation of a computing problem to executable programs."}
{"uri":"topic_3373","label":"Drug development","definition":"The process of bringing a new drug to market once a lead compounds has been identified through drug discovery."}
{"uri":"topic_3374","label":"Biotherapeutics","definition":"The process of formulating and administering a pharmaceutical compound to achieve a therapeutic effect."}
{"uri":"topic_3375","label":"Drug metabolism","definition":"The study of how a drug interacts with the body."}
{"uri":"topic_3376","label":"Medicines research and development","definition":"The discovery, development and approval of medicines."}
{"uri":"topic_3377","label":"Safety sciences","definition":"The safety (or lack) of drugs and other medical interventions."}
{"uri":"topic_3378","label":"Pharmacovigilance","definition":"The detection, assessment, understanding and prevention of adverse effects of medicines."}
{"uri":"topic_3379","label":"Preclinical and clinical studies","definition":"The testing of new medicines, vaccines or procedures on animals (preclinical) and humans (clinical) prior to their approval by regulatory authorities."}
{"uri":"topic_3382","label":"Imaging","definition":"The visual representation of an object."}
{"uri":"topic_3383","label":"Bioimaging","definition":"The use of imaging techniques to understand biology."}
{"uri":"topic_3384","label":"Medical imaging","definition":"The use of imaging techniques for clinical purposes for medical research."}
{"uri":"topic_3385","label":"Light microscopy","definition":"The use of optical instruments to magnify the image of an object."}
{"uri":"topic_3386","label":"Laboratory animal science","definition":"The use of animals and alternatives in experimental research."}
{"uri":"topic_3387","label":"Marine biology","definition":"The study of organisms in the ocean or brackish waters."}
{"uri":"topic_3388","label":"Molecular medicine","definition":"The identification of molecular and genetic causes of disease and the development of interventions to correct them."}
{"uri":"topic_3390","label":"Nutritional science","definition":"The study of the effects of food components on the metabolism, health, performance and disease resistance of humans and animals. It also includes the study of human behaviours related to food choices."}
{"uri":"topic_3391","label":"Omics","definition":"The collective characterisation and quantification of pools of biological molecules that translate into the structure, function, and dynamics of an organism or organisms."}
{"uri":"topic_3393","label":"Quality affairs","definition":"The processes that need to be in place to ensure the quality of products for human or animal use."}
{"uri":"topic_3394","label":"Regulatory affairs","definition":"The protection of public health by controlling the safety and efficacy of products in areas including pharmaceuticals, veterinary medicine, medical devices, pesticides, agrochemicals, cosmetics, and complementary medicines."}
{"uri":"topic_3395","label":"Regenerative medicine","definition":"Biomedical approaches to clinical interventions that involve the use of stem cells."}
{"uri":"topic_3396","label":"Systems medicine","definition":"An interdisciplinary field of study that looks at the dynamic systems of the human body as part of an integrted whole, incorporating biochemical, physiological, and environmental interactions that sustain life."}
{"uri":"topic_3397","label":"Veterinary medicine","definition":"Topic concerning the branch of medicine that deals with the prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of disease, disorder and injury in animals."}
{"uri":"topic_3398","label":"Bioengineering","definition":"The application of biological concepts and methods to the analytical and synthetic methodologies of engineering."}
{"uri":"topic_3399","label":"Geriatric medicine","definition":"The branch of medicine dealing with the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of disease in older people, and the problems specific to aging."}
{"uri":"topic_3400","label":"Allergy, clinical immunology and immunotherapeutics","definition":"Health issues related to the immune system and their prevention, diagnosis and management."}
{"uri":"topic_3401","label":"Pain medicine","definition":"The prevention of pain and the evaluation, treatment and rehabilitation of persons in pain."}
{"uri":"topic_3402","label":"Anaesthesiology","definition":"Anaesthesia and anaesthetics."}
{"uri":"topic_3403","label":"Critical care medicine","definition":"The multidisciplinary that cares for patients with acute, life-threatening illness or injury."}
{"uri":"topic_3404","label":"Dermatology","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with prevention, diagnosis and treatment of disorders of the skin, scalp, hair and nails."}
{"uri":"topic_3405","label":"Dentistry","definition":"The study, diagnosis, prevention and treatments of disorders of the oral cavity, maxillofacial area and adjacent structures."}
{"uri":"topic_3406","label":"Ear, nose and throat medicine","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of disorders of the ear, nose and throat."}
{"uri":"topic_3407","label":"Endocrinology and metabolism","definition":"The branch of medicine dealing with diseases of endocrine organs, hormone systems, their target organs, and disorders of the pathways of glucose and lipid metabolism."}
{"uri":"topic_3408","label":"Haematology","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the blood, blood-forming organs and blood diseases."}
{"uri":"topic_3409","label":"Gastroenterology","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with disorders of the oesophagus, stomach, duodenum, jejenum, ileum, large intestine, sigmoid colon and rectum."}
{"uri":"topic_3410","label":"Gender medicine","definition":"The study of the biological and physiological differences between males and females and how they effect differences in disease presentation and management."}
{"uri":"topic_3411","label":"Gynaecology and obstetrics","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the health of the female reproductive system, pregnancy and birth."}
{"uri":"topic_3412","label":"Hepatic and biliary medicine","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the liver, gallbladder, bile ducts and bile."}
{"uri":"topic_3414","label":"Trauma medicine","definition":"The branch of medicine that treats body wounds or shock produced by sudden physical injury, as from violence or accident."}
{"uri":"topic_3415","label":"Medical toxicology","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the diagnosis, management and prevention of poisoning and other adverse health effects caused by medications, occupational and environmental toxins, and biological agents."}
{"uri":"topic_3416","label":"Musculoskeletal medicine","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of disorders of the muscle, bone and connective tissue. It incorporates aspects of orthopaedics, rheumatology, rehabilitation medicine and pain medicine."}
{"uri":"topic_3417","label":"Ophthalmology","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with disorders of the eye, including eyelid, optic nerve/visual pathways and occular muscles."}
{"uri":"topic_3418","label":"Paediatrics","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the medical care of infants, children and adolescents."}
{"uri":"topic_3419","label":"Psychiatry","definition":"The branch of medicine that deals with the management of mental illness, emotional disturbance and abnormal behaviour."}
{"uri":"topic_3420","label":"Reproductive health","definition":"The health of the reproductive processes, functions and systems at all stages of life."}
{"uri":"topic_3421","label":"Surgery","definition":"The use of operative, manual and instrumental techniques on a patient to investigate and/or treat a pathological condition or help improve bodily function or appearance."}
{"uri":"topic_3422","label":"Urology and nephrology","definition":"The branches of medicine and physiology focussing on the function and disorders of the urinary system in males and females, the reproductive system in males, and the kidney."}
{"uri":"topic_3423","label":"Complementary medicine","definition":"Medical therapies that fall beyond the scope of conventional medicine but may be used alongside it in the treatment of disease and ill health."}
{"uri":"topic_3444","label":"MRI","definition":"Techniques that uses magnetic fields and radiowaves to form images, typically to investigate the anatomy and physiology of the human body."}
{"uri":"topic_3448","label":"Neutron diffraction","definition":"The study of matter by studying the diffraction pattern from firing neutrons at a sample, typically to determine atomic and/or magnetic structure."}
{"uri":"topic_3452","label":"Tomography","definition":"Imaging in sections (sectioning), through the use of a wave-generating device (tomograph) that generates an image (a tomogram)."}
{"uri":"topic_3473","label":"Data mining","definition":"The discovery of patterns in large data sets and the extraction and trasnsformation of those patterns into a useful format."}
{"uri":"topic_3474","label":"Machine learning","definition":"A topic concerning the application of artificial intelligence methods to algorithms, in order to create methods that can learn from data in order to generate an output, rather than relying on explicitly encoded information only."}
{"uri":"topic_3489","label":"Database management","definition":"The general handling of data stored in digital archives such as databases, databanks, web portals, and other data resources."}
{"uri":"topic_3500","label":"Zoology","definition":"Animals, e.g. information on a specific animal genome including molecular sequences, genes and annotation."}
{"uri":"topic_3510","label":"Protein sites, features and motifs","definition":"The biology, archival, detection, prediction and analysis of positional features such as functional and other key sites, in protein sequences and the conserved patterns (motifs, profiles etc.) that may be used to describe them."}
{"uri":"topic_3511","label":"Nucleic acid sites, features and motifs","definition":"The biology, archival, detection, prediction and analysis of positional features such as functional and other key sites, in nucleic acid sequences and the conserved patterns (motifs, profiles etc.) that may be used to describe them."}
{"uri":"topic_3512","label":"Gene transcripts","definition":"Transcription of DNA into RNA and features of a messenger RNA (mRNA) molecules including precursor RNA, primary (unprocessed) transcript and fully processed molecules."}
{"uri":"topic_3516","label":"Genotyping experiment","definition":"Genotype experiment including case control, population, and family studies. These might use array based methods and re-sequencing methods."}
{"uri":"topic_3517","label":"GWAS study","definition":"Genome-wide association study experiments."}
{"uri":"topic_3518","label":"Microarray experiment","definition":"Microarray experiments including conditions, protocol, sample:data relationships etc."}
{"uri":"topic_3519","label":"PCR experiment","definition":"PCR experiments, e.g. quantitative real-time PCR."}
{"uri":"topic_3520","label":"Proteomics experiment","definition":"Proteomics experiments."}
{"uri":"topic_3523","label":"RNAi experiment","definition":"Experiment in which the expression of a specific gene is post-transcriptionally knocked down or silenced by means of a small RNA (sRNA) causing the degradation of the gene transcript (mRNA), and thus preventing the production of the corresponding protein."}
{"uri":"topic_3524","label":"Simulation experiment","definition":"Biological computational model experiments (simulation), for example the minimum information required in order to permit its correct interpretation and reproduction."}
{"uri":"topic_3534","label":"Protein binding sites","definition":"Binding sites in proteins, including cleavage sites (for a proteolytic enzyme or agent), key residues involved in protein folding, catalytic residues (active site) of an enzyme, ligand-binding (non-catalytic) residues of a protein, such as sites that bind metal, prosthetic groups or lipids, RNA and DNA-binding proteins and binding sites etc."}
{"uri":"topic_3538","label":"Protein disordered structure","definition":"Disordered structure in a protein."}
{"uri":"topic_3542","label":"Protein secondary structure","definition":"Secondary structure (predicted or real) of a protein, including super-secondary structure."}
{"uri":"topic_3569","label":"Applied mathematics","definition":"The application of mathematics to specific problems in science, typically by the formulation and analysis of mathematical models."}
{"uri":"topic_3570","label":"Pure mathematics","definition":"The study of abstract mathematical concepts."}
{"uri":"topic_3571","label":"Data governance","definition":"Data governance is the control of data entry and maintenance to ensure the data meets defined standards, qualities, or constraints."}
{"uri":"topic_3572","label":"Data quality management","definition":"The quality, integrity, and cleaning up of data."}
{"uri":"topic_3573","label":"Freshwater biology","definition":"The study of organisms in freshwater ecosystems."}
{"uri":"topic_3574","label":"Human genetics","definition":"The study of inheritance in human beings."}
{"uri":"topic_3575","label":"Tropical medicine","definition":"Health problems that are prevalent in tropical and subtropical regions."}
{"uri":"topic_3576","label":"Medical biotechnology","definition":"Biotechnology applied to the medical sciences and the development of medicines."}
{"uri":"topic_3577","label":"Personalised medicine","definition":"An approach to medicine whereby decisions, practices and are tailored to the individual patient based on their predicted response or risk of disease."}
{"uri":"topic_3656","label":"Immunoprecipitation experiment","definition":"Experimental techniques to purify a protein-DNA crosslinked complex. Usually sequencing follows e.g. in the techniques ChIP-chip, ChIP-seq and MeDIP-seq."}
{"uri":"topic_3673","label":"Whole genome sequencing","definition":"Laboratory technique to sequence the complete DNA sequence of an organism's genome at a single time."}
{"uri":"topic_3674","label":"Methylated DNA immunoprecipitation","definition":"Laboratory technique to sequence the methylated regions in DNA."}
{"uri":"topic_3676","label":"Exome sequencing","definition":"Laboratory technique to sequence all the protein-coding regions in a genome, i.e., the exome."}
{"uri":"topic_3678","label":"Experimental design and studies","definition":"The design of an experiment intended to test a hypothesis, and describe or explain empirical data obtained under various experimental conditions."}
{"uri":"topic_3679","label":"Animal study","definition":"The design of an experiment involving non-human animals."}
{"uri":"topic_3697","label":"Microbial ecology","definition":"The ecology of microorganisms including their relationship with one another and their environment."}
{"uri":"topic_3794","label":"RNA immunoprecipitation","definition":"An antibody-based technique used to map in vivo RNA-protein interactions."}
{"uri":"topic_3796","label":"Population genomics","definition":"Large-scale study (typically comparison) of DNA sequences of populations."}
{"uri":"topic_3810","label":"Agricultural science","definition":"Multidisciplinary study, research and development within the field of agriculture."}
{"uri":"topic_3837","label":"Metagenomic sequencing","definition":"Approach which samples, in parallel, all genes in all organisms present in a given sample, e.g. to provide insight into biodiversity and function."}
{"uri":"topic_3855","label":"Environmental sciences","definition":"Study of the environment, the interactions between its physical, chemical, and biological components and it's effect on life. Also how humans impact upon the environment, and how we can manage and utilise natural resources."}
{"uri":"topic_3892","label":"Biomolecular simulation","definition":"The study and simulation of molecular conformations using a computational model and computer simulations."}
{"uri":"topic_3895","label":"Synthetic biology","definition":"The application of multi-disciplinary science and technology for the construction of artificial biological systems for diverse applications."}
{"uri":"topic_3912","label":"Genetic engineering","definition":"The application of biotechnology to directly manipulate an organism's genes."}
{"uri":"topic_3922","label":"Proteogenomics","definition":"A field of biological research focused on the discovery and identification of peptides, typically by comparing mass spectra against a protein database."}
{"uri":"topic_3923","label":"Genome resequencing","definition":"Laboratory experiment to identify the differences between a specific genome (of an individual) and a reference genome (developed typically from many thousands of individuals). WGS re-sequencing is used as golden standard to detect variations compared to a given reference genome, including small variants (SNP and InDels) as well as larger genome re-organisations (CNVs, translocations, etc.)."}
{"uri":"topic_3930","label":"Immunogenetics","definition":"A biomedical field that bridges immunology and genetics, to study the genetic basis of the immune system."}
{"uri":"topic_3931","label":"Chemometrics","definition":"Interdisciplinary science focused on extracting information from chemical systems by data analytical approaches, for example multivariate statistics, applied mathematics, and computer science."}
{"uri":"topic_3934","label":"Cytometry","definition":"Cytometry is the measurement of the characteristics of cells."}
{"uri":"topic_3939","label":"Metabolic engineering","definition":"Biotechnology approach that seeks to optimize cellular genetic and regulatory processes in order to increase the cells' production of a certain substance."}
{"uri":"topic_3940","label":"Chromosome conformation capture","definition":"Molecular biology methods used to analyze the spatial organization of chromatin in a cell."}
{"uri":"topic_3941","label":"Metatranscriptomics","definition":"The study of microbe gene expression within natural environments (i.e. the metatranscriptome)."}
{"uri":"topic_3943","label":"Paleogenomics","definition":"The reconstruction and analysis of genomic information in extinct species."}
{"uri":"topic_3944","label":"Cladistics","definition":"The biological classification of organisms by categorizing them in groups (\"clades\") based on their most recent common ancestor."}
{"uri":"topic_3945","label":"Molecular evolution","definition":"The study of the process and mechanism of change of biomolecules such as DNA, RNA, and proteins across generations."}
{"uri":"topic_3948","label":"Immunoinformatics","definition":"Immunoinformatics is the field of computational biology that deals with the study of immunoloogical questions. Immunoinformatics is at the interface between immunology and computer science. It takes advantage of computational, statistical, mathematical approaches and enhances the understanding of immunological knowledge."}
{"uri":"topic_3954","label":"Echography","definition":"A diagnostic imaging technique based on the application of ultrasound."}
{"uri":"topic_3955","label":"Fluxomics","definition":"Experimental approaches to determine the rates of metabolic reactions - the metabolic fluxes - within a biological entity."}
{"uri":"topic_3957","label":"Protein interaction experiment","definition":"An experiment for studying protein-protein interactions."}
{"uri":"topic_3958","label":"Copy number variation","definition":"A DNA structural variation, specifically a duplication or deletion event, resulting in sections of the genome to be repeated, or the number of repeats in the genome to vary between individuals."}
{"uri":"topic_3959","label":"Cytogenetics","definition":"The branch of genetics concerned with the relationships between chromosomes and cellular behaviour, especially during mitosis and meiosis."}
{"uri":"topic_3966","label":"Vaccinology","definition":"The design of vaccines to protect against a particular pathogen, including antigens, delivery systems, and adjuvants to elicit a predictable immune response against specific epitopes."}
{"uri":"topic_3967","label":"Immunomics","definition":"The study of immune system as a whole, its regulation and response to pathogens using genome-wide approaches."}
{"uri":"topic_3974","label":"Epistasis","definition":"Epistasis can be defined as the ability of the genotype at one locus to supersede the phenotypic effect of a mutation at another locus. This interaction between genes can occur at different level: gene expression, protein levels, etc..."}
{"uri":"topic_4010","label":"Open science","definition":"Open science encompasses the practices of making scientific research transparent and participatory, and its outputs publicly accessible."}
{"uri":"topic_4011","label":"Data rescue","definition":"Data rescue denotes digitalisation, formatting, archival, and publication of data that were not available in accessible or usable form. Examples are data from private archives, data inside publications, or in paper records stored privately or publicly."}
{"uri":"topic_4012","label":"FAIR data","definition":"FAIR data is scientific data that meets the principles of being findable, accessible, interoperable, and reusable."}
{"uri":"topic_4013","label":"Antimicrobial resistance","definition":"Microbial mechanisms for protecting microorganisms against antimicrobial agents."}
{"uri":"topic_4014","label":"Electroencephalography","definition":"The monitoring method for measuring electrical activity in the brain."}
{"uri":"topic_4016","label":"Electrocardiography","definition":"The monitoring method for measuring electrical activity in the heart."}
{"uri":"topic_4017","label":"Cryogenic electron microscopy","definition":"A method for studying biomolecules and other structures at very low (cryogenic) temperature using electron microscopy."}
{"uri":"topic_4019","label":"Biosciences","definition":"Biosciences, or life sciences, include fields of study related to life, living beings, and biomolecules."}
{"uri":"topic_4020","label":"Carbon cycle","definition":"The carbon cycle is the biogeochemical pathway of carbon moving through the different parts of the Earth (such as ocean, atmosphere, soil), or eventually another planet."}
{"uri":"topic_4021","label":"Multiomics","definition":"Multiomics concerns integration of data from multiple omics (e.g. transcriptomics, proteomics, epigenomics)."}
{"uri":"topic_4027","label":"Ribosome Profiling","definition":"With ribosome profiling, ribosome-protected mRNA fragments are analyzed with RNA-seq techniques leading to a genome-wide measurement of the translation landscape."}
{"uri":"topic_4028","label":"Single-cell sequencing","definition":"Combined with NGS (Next Generation Sequencing) technologies, single-cell sequencing allows the study of genetic information (DNA, RNA, epigenome...) at a single cell level. It is often used for differential analysis and gene expression profiling."}
{"uri":"topic_4029","label":"Acoustics","definition":"The study of mechanical waves in liquids, solids, and gases."}
{"uri":"topic_4030","label":"Microfluidics","definition":"Interdisplinary study of behavior, precise control, and manipulation of low (microlitre) volume fluids in constrained space."}
{"uri":"topic_4037","label":"Genomic imprinting","definition":"Genomic imprinting is a gene regulation mechanism by which a subset of genes are expressed from one of the two parental chromosomes only. Imprinted genes are organized in clusters, their silencing/activation of the imprinted loci involves epigenetic marks (DNA methylation, etc) and so-called imprinting control regions (ICR). It has been described in mammals, but also plants and insects."}
{"uri":"topic_4038","label":"Metabarcoding","definition":"Metabarcoding is the barcoding of (environmental) DNA or RNA to identify multiple taxa from the same sample."}
{"uri":"topic_4044","label":"Data protection","definition":"Data protection is a topic concerning data that should be protected from disclosure, damage, or unauthorised access, due to its sensitive nature."}
{"uri":"topic_4045","label":"Cybersecurity","definition":"Cybersecurity is a topic comprising the approaches and technologies that enable the protection of computer systems, networks and programs from digital attacks. It ensures the availability, integrity, and confidentiality of processed and stored information."}
{"uri":"topic_4046","label":"Version control","definition":"Version control is a technology for consistent management, storing, and sharing of evolving versions of digital artefacts, such as computer programs, scripts, documents, data, or media files."}
{"uri":"topic_4047","label":"Software management","definition":"Software management comprises the practices and principles of taking care of software and software-based or software-like services, other than programming and maintenance. This includes for example taking care of the associated information and documentation, and the processes of contribution, validation, release/publication, or deployment."}
{"uri":"topic_4051","label":"ChIP-exo","definition":"Chromatin immunoprecipitation-based exeperiment similar to ChIP-seq, with an additional experimental step using an exonuclease to increase the resolution of protein binding site identification."}
{"uri":"topic_4052","label":"Hi-C","definition":"High-throughput genomic and epigenomic technique that capture chromatin conformation, allowing a genome-wide identification of chromatin interactions and structure."}
{"uri":"topic_4053","label":"ATAC-seq","definition":"Assay for Transposase-Accessible Chromatin with high throughput sequencing. This technique is designed for the genome-wide detection of open chromatin regions."}
{"uri":"topic_4054","label":"miRNA silencing","definition":"Experiment in which the expression of a given gene is knocked down by means of a micro RNA (miRNA) causing the degradation of the gene transcript (mRNA)."}
{"uri":"topic_4055","label":"siRNA experiment","definition":"Experiment in which the expression of a given gene is knocked down by means of a small interfering RNA (siRNA) causing the degradation of the gene transcript (mRNA)."}
{"uri":"topic_4056","label":"Long-read sequencing","definition":"Long-read sequencing is a sequencing method that produces reads thousands to millions of base pairs long, allowing for better resolution of complex regions, structural variants, and full-length transcripts."}
{"uri":"topic_4057","label":"Short-read sequencing","definition":"Short-read sequencing is a high-throughput sequencing method that generates millions of short nucleotide fragments, typically 50–300 base pairs in length."}
{"uri":"topic_4060","label":"Metaproteomics","definition":"Metaproteomics is the profiling of proteins in a sample that contains material from multiple species or strains of organisms."}
{"uri":"topic_4061","label":"Bisulfite sequencing","definition":"Bisulfite sequencing is a sequencing technique used to determine DNA methylation patterns by treating DNA with bisulfite, which converts unmethylated cytosines to uracils while leaving methylated cytosines unchanged."}
{"uri":"topic_4062","label":"Bulk RNA barcoding and sequencing","definition":"Bulk RNA barcoding and sequencing (BRB-seq) is a highly mutliplexed bulk RNA-Seq technique where each RNA sample gets a barcode, and many samples are sequenced together."}
{"uri":"topic_4063","label":"DNase sequencing","definition":"DNase sequencing is a technique used to identify regions of open chromatin by sequencing DNA fragments generated after treatment with DNase I, which preferentially cuts accessible DNA."}
{"uri":"topic_4064","label":"MicroRNA sequencing","definition":"Specific sequencing of small RNAs using a variant of RNA-seq, with an additional fragment size selection step."}
{"uri":"topic_4065","label":"Exposomics","definition":"Exposomics is the systematic and comprehensive study of the exposome and the associated biological responses (exposure-phenotype interaction). Exposome is the totality of environmental exposures, that is, the cumulative (e.g. life-long) totality of contacts between external factors (e.g. chemical agents) and a living organism, a population, or a biological taxon."}
